RESOLUTION NO. 307-26
EXPRESSING THE SUPPORT AND ENDORSEMENT OF THE SANGGUNIANG BAYAN OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, FOR THE ESTABLISHMENT OF STA. CRUZ SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL, AS A STAND-ALONE SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL IN THE MUNICIPALITY
Authored and Sponsored by: Hon. JULIUS FRENCIE MENDOZA RIZADA
Co-Sponsored by: All SB Members present
PRESENT:
• Hon. Charlotte F. Gallego – Vice-Mayor
• Hon. Apolinar C. Ugdoracion, Jr.
• Hon. Sharmaine Fe L. Mole
• Hon. Roche S. Cabanda
• Hon. Anselmo A. Datu
• Hon. Alvin Rey C. Almendras
• Hon. Julius Frencie M. Rizada
• Hon. Manolito R. Lagrada, Jr.
• Hon. Kristeen Pearl D. Cahiles – SKMF President
• Hon. Danilo A. Baquial – Liga Ng Barangay President
• Hon. Elvira I. Lim – IP Mandatory Representative
ABSENT:
• Hon. Michelle O. Orpilla (OL)
WHEREAS, the Constitution of the Republic of the Philippines recognizes the right of all citizens to quality education and directs the State to establish, maintain, and support a complete, adequate, and integrated system of education responsive to the needs of the people and society;
WHEREAS, Republic Act No. 10533, otherwise known as the "Enhanced Basic Education Act of 2013," institutionalized the K to 12 Basic Education Program, including Senior High School, with the objective of providing learners with the necessary competencies and preparing them for higher education, employment, entrepreneurship, and middle-level skills development;
WHEREAS, the Department of Education issued DepEd Order No. 51, s. 2015, entitled "Guidelines on the Implementation of the Senior High School (SHS) Program in Existing Public Junior High Schools (JHSs) and Integrated Schools (ISs), Establishment of Stand-Alone Public SHSs, and Conversion of Existing Public Elementary and JHSs into Stand-Alone SHSs," which provides the guidelines, requirements, procedures, and criteria for the establishment of stand-alone public Senior High Schools;
WHEREAS, DepEd Order No. 26, s. 2017, entitled "Addendum to DepEd Order No. 51, s. 2015," amended certain provisions of the foregoing guidelines, including the procedures for the certification and confirmation of stand-alone public Senior High Schools;
WHEREAS, the proposed establishment of a stand-alone Senior High School to be known as "Sta. Cruz Senior High School" is intended to expand access to Senior High School education within the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur and provide learners with accessible, relevant, and quality secondary education responsive to their educational needs and future academic, employment, entrepreneurial, and skills-development opportunities;
WHEREAS, the proposed Sta. Cruz Senior High School offered the following tracks and clusters to provide learners with opportunities to pursue academic advancement, acquire technical and professional competencies, and prepare for employment, entrepreneurship, and further education:
a. Academic Track, consisting of the following clusters:
1. Arts, Social Sciences and Humanities (ASSH);
2. Business and Entrepreneurship (BE); and
3. Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM);
b. Technical-Professional (TechPro) Track, consisting of the following clusters:
1. Aesthetic, Wellness and Human Care;
2. Hospitality and Tourism;
3. Information and Communication Technology (ICT);
4. Construction and Building Technologies; and
5. Industrial Technologies;
WHEREAS, the proposed establishment of a Stand-Alone Senior High School was duly endorsed and supported by the Local School Board (LSB) of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz and the School Parents-Teachers Association (SPTA) of Sta. Cruz National High School (SCNHS), as evidenced by LSB Resolution No. 4, s. 2026 and SPTA Resolution No. 001, s. 2026, respectively;
WHEREAS, such endorsements reflect the support of the local education stakeholders and the parents and teachers of the existing Senior High School program for the establishment of a separate and independent Senior High School in the Municipality;
WHEREAS, the establishment of the proposed Sta. Cruz Senior High School is consistent with the Municipality's continuing commitment to support education and human resource development and is responsive to the educational needs and development priorities of the Municipality;
WHEREAS, the establishment of the proposed Sta. Cruz Senior High School remains subject to the evaluation, assessment, and approval of the Department of Education in accordance with DepEd Order No. 51, s. 2015, as amended by DepEd Order No. 26, s. 2017, and other applicable DepEd policies, rules, regulations, standards, and requirements;
WHEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Julius Frencie M. Rizada, duly seconded by Hon. Sharmaine Fe L. Mole, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to EXPRESS THE SUPPORT AND ENDORSEMENT OF THE SANGGUNIANG BAYAN OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, FOR THE ESTABLISHMENT OF STA. CRUZ SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL, AS A STAND-ALONE SENIOR HIGH SCHOOL IN THE MUNICIPALITY;
RESOLVED FURTHER, to respectfully endorse and transmit this Resolution to the Schools Division Office of Davao del Sur and other appropriate offices of the Department of Education as part of the documentary requirements for the evaluation and processing of the proposed establishment of the stand-alone Sta. Cruz Senior High School;
RESOLVED FINALLY, that copies of this Resolution be furnished to other concerned offices for their information and appropriate action.
APPROVED, by a unanimous vote of all members of the Sangguniang Bayan present.
CERTIFIED CORRECT:
MICHAEL RYAN D. BAJO
Secretary to the Sanggunian
ATTESTED:
ATTY. CHARLOTTE F. GALLEGO
Municipal Vice-Mayor (Presiding Officer)

