# ENACTING AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE LOCAL YOUTH DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (LYDD) OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS, AND CREATING A PLANTILLA POSITION THEREIN
WHEREAS, Section 25 of Republic Act No. 10742, otherwise known as the Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) Reform Act of 2015, and its Implementing Rules and Regulations provide for the creation of a Youth Development Office in every province, city, and municipality;
WHEREAS, said law provides that the Local Youth Development Office (LYDO) shall be headed by a Youth Development Officer with the rank of at least division chief, and may be placed under the Local Chief Executive (LCE), the Office of Planning and Development, the Office of Social Welfare, or any other office deemed appropriate by the Local Government Unit (LGU);
WHEREAS, Memorandum Circular No. 2017-36 issued by the Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) dated February 24, 2017, directed Provincial Governors, City and Municipal Mayors to create their respective LYDOs within their areas of jurisdiction;
WHEREAS, Section 76 of Republic Act No. 7160, otherwise known as the Local Government Code, recognizes the power of LGUs to design and implement their own organizational structure and staffing pattern, taking into account service requirements and financial capability, subject to the minimum standards and guidelines prescribed by the Civil Service Commission;
WHEREAS, this legislative measure will greatly aid the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Province of Davao del Sur, in the effective implementation of the foregoing laws and directives for the benefit and development of its youth sector;
NOW THEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Kristeen Pearl D. Cahiles, duly seconded by Hon. Sharmaine Fe L. Mole, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session, to enact the following ordinance:
