# MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 04
# Series of 2025
# AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE LOCAL YOUTH DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (LYDD) OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS AND CREATING ONE PLANTILLA POSITION THEREIN
Be it ordained by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, in session assembled that:
SECTION 1. TITLE. This Ordinance shall be known as the Municipal Youth Development Division (LYDD) Ordinance of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur.
SECTION 2. DECLARATION OF POLICY. It is the policy of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur to promote and ensure the development and empowerment of the youth sector by institutionalizing a Local Youth Development Division tasked with implementing youth-focused programs and services.
SECTION 3. ESTABLISHMENT OF THE LOCAL YOUTH DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (LYDD). There is hereby created the Local Youth Development Division within the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, which shall be responsible for the planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of youth development programs and initiatives.
SECTION 4. OBJECTIVES OF THE LOCAL YOUTH DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (LYDD). The LYDD shall aim to:
- Empower youth by providing platforms for leadership and civic engagement;
Develop and sustain programs that address youth needs and aspirations;
- Enhance youth participation in local governance;
- Promote youth welfare by addressing concerns in education, employment, health, and social services.
SECTION 5. FUNCTIONS OF THE LOCAL YOUTH DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (LYDD). The LYDD shall:
1. Register and verify youth and youth-serving organizations in accordance with Section 24(d) of the SK Reform Act of 2015 and the Youth Organizations' Registration Guidelines;
2. Provide technical assistance to the Local Youth Development Council (LYDC) in the formulation of the Local Youth Development Plan (LYDP);
3. Facilitate the election of LYDC representatives;
4. Serve as secretariat to the LYDC;
5. Conduct mandatory and continuing training for SK officials and LYDC members, pursuant to programs designed by the National Youth Commission (NYC) and the DILG. The Local Youth Development Officer or authorized staff shall secure accreditation from the NYC to conduct such training;
6. Provide technical, logistical, and other support for the conduct of mandatory training and other programs of the NYC and DILG;
7. Coordinate with the National Youth Commission on youth programs within the LGU's jurisdiction;
8. Monitor and document the implementation of SK programs and activities within the municipality, ensuring alignment with the LYDP and compliance with relevant laws, in coordination with the LYDC and DILG;
9. Perform other functions as may be prescribed by law, ordinance, or as directed by the LCE, DILG, or NYC.
SECTION 6. CREATION OF PLANTILLA POSITION. In pursuance of Section 76 of RA 7160, the plantilla of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur is hereby reorganized to include the Local Youth Development Division under the Office of the Mayor. Consequently, one (1) Youth Development Officer III (SG 18) position shall be created.
Municipal Ordinance No. 04 | Page 2
# SECTION 7. MINIMUM QUALIFICATION STANDARDS.
| POSITION TITLE | EDUCATION | ELIGIBILITY | RELEVANT EXPERIENCE | RELEVANT TRAINING |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Youth Development Officer III (SG 18) | Bachelor's Degree | Career Service Professional / 2nd Level Eligibility | Minimum 2 years | At least 8 hours |
SECTION 8. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES. The Youth Development Officer III shall:
A. Oversee the development and implementation of youth-related programs fostering leadership and skills development;
B. Develop, promote, and monitor policies, plans, programs, and services for youth development in coordination with relevant agencies;
C. Register and verify youth and youth-serving organizations under the Youth Organizations' Registration Program (YORP)
D. Provide technical assistance to the LYDC in the formulation of the LYDP;
E. Facilitate the election of LYDC representatives;
F. Serve as secretariat to the LYDC;
G. Conduct mandatory and continuing training for SK officials and LYDC members, in coordination with NYC and DILG;
H. Provide technical and logistical support for training programs and other NYC and DILG initiatives;
I. Coordinate with the NYC regarding youth programs within the LGU;
J. Monitor and document the implementation of SK activities and programs, ensuring compliance and alignment with the LYDP;
K. Ensure timely preparation and submission of reports;
L. Perform other tasks as directed by the immediate supervisor or the LCE.
SECTION 9. APPROPRIATIONS. The budget for the salaries of the plantilla position and operating expenses of the LYDD shall be included in the annual municipal appropriations.
SECTION 10. SEPARABILITY CLAUSE. If any section or provision of this Ordinance is declared unconstitutional or invalid, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
SECTION 11. REPEALING CLAUSE. This Ordinance hereby amends Municipal Ordinance No. 08, Series of 2014, or the Revised Organizational Structure and Staffing Pattern of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, as amended.
SECTION 12. EFFECTIVITY. This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon approval.
ENACTED, this 25th day of June 2025, by a unanimous vote of all members of the Sangguniang Bayan during its 111th Regular Session.
