ENACTING AN ORDINANCE AMENDING MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 13, SERIES OF 2020, PROVIDING FOR THE UPGRADING OF THE PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT SERVICE OFFICE (PESO) TO A REGULAR DEPARTMENT OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, CREATING THE POSITION OF DEPARTMENT HEAD AS A PLANTILLA POSITION, AND APPROPRIATING FUNDS THEREFOR
WHEREAS, Municipal Ordinance No. 13, Series of 2020, established the Public Employment Service Office (PESO) in the Municipality of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur, to provide employment facilitation and related services to the local labor force;
WHEREAS, Civil Service Commission Memorandum Circular No. 12, Series of 2022, mandates the institutionalization of mandatory plantilla positions and upgrading of local government offices to full-fledged departments where appropriate;
WHEREAS, the Municipal Government of Santa Cruz, through the Office of the Municipal Mayor, submitted an Executive Proposal recommending the upgrading of the PESO to a regular department and the creation of a Department Head position to strengthen operational capacity and enhance service delivery;
WHEREAS, the proposed amendment seeks to harmonize existing legislation with national policies, improve internal management, and ensure more effective employment facilitation at the local level;
WHEREAS, it is necessary to amend Municipal Ordinance No. 13, Series of 2020, to reflect said structural and operational changes for the continued improvement of public employment services in the Municipality;
WHEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Sharmaine Fe L. Mole, unanimously seconded, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to enact the following:
MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 05
Series of 2025
SECTION 1. TITLE.
This Ordinance shall be known and cited as:
"An Ordinance Upgrading the Public Employment Service Office (PESO) as a Regular Department of the Municipality of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur."
Municipal Ordinance No. 05 | Page 1
# SECTION 2. DECLARATION OF POLICY (Amending Section 2 of Ordinance No. 13, s. 2020)
In furtherance of the objectives of Republic Act No. 8759, otherwise known as the "Public Employment Service Office Act of 1999," and in line with Civil Service Commission Memorandum Circular No. 12, Series of 2022, the Municipality of Santa Cruz affirms its commitment to institutionalize PESO as a permanent and integral department within the local government structure to strengthen the delivery of employment facilitation and labor market information services.
# SECTION 3. ESTABLISHMENT OF PESO AS A REGULAR DEPARTMENT
The Public Employment Service Office (PESO), previously established under Municipal Ordinance No. 13, Series of 2020, is hereby upgraded and reconstituted as a regular department of the Municipal Government of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur.
# SECTION 4. FUNCTIONS OF THE PESO (Amending Section 3 of Ordinance No. 13, s. 2020)
The PESO shall perform the following functions:
1. Encourage employers to regularly submit to the PESO a list of job vacancies in their respective establishments, in order to facilitate the exchange of labor market information services to job seekers, both for local and overseas employment, and recruitment assistance to employers;
2. Develop and administer testing and evaluation instruments for effective job selection, training and counseling;
3. Provide persons with entrepreneurship qualities access to various livelihood and self-employment programs offered by both government and non-government organizations at the provincial/ cities/ municipal/ barangay levels by undertaking referrals for such programs;
4. Undertake employability enhancement trainings/ seminars for job seekers, as well as for those who would like to change careers or enhance their employability, in coordination with the Municipal Skills Training Center;
5. Provide employment and occupational counseling, career coaching, mass motivation and values development activities;
6. Conduct pre-employment counseling and orientation to prospective local and overseas workers;
7. Provide reintegration assistance services to returning Filipino migrant workers;
8. Collect employment data and develop qualitative statistical indicators to facilitate the assessment of employment-related activities. It shall also serve as the data bank of the municipal government on Public Employment Services;
9. Endeavor to look for market of local products and services and to provide for skill-product matching and technical support;
10. Create linkages and partnerships with non-government organizations and civil society organizations;
11. Coordinate with the different barangays in the Municipality for the inventory of skilled workers and professionals and transmit information to them relative to job vacancies and other employment services to job seekers;
12. Encourage and assist the barangays within the Municipality to create Barangay Employment Assistance Center;
13. Promote equal opportunity employment for qualified differently-abled persons;
14. Promote equal rights to employment regardless of gender and sexual preferences;
15. Prepare and submit to the local sanggunian an annual employment plan and budget including other regular funding sources and budgetary support of the PESO;
16. Perform such function which willfully carry out the objectives of this Ordinance.
17. Manage technical and administrative operations of the PESO;
18. Identify training needs and oversee capacity building;
19. Enforce internal discipline and staff coaching;
20. Maintain efficient internal office systems;
21. Conduct procedural reviews for efficiency;
22. Maintain communication with the Local Chief Executive for policy alignment;
23. Perform related duties as may be assigned by the LCE or immediate supervisor.
Municipal Ordinance No. 05 | Page 2
# SECTION 5. CREATION OF PLANTILLA POSITION (Amending Section 4 of Ordinance No. 13. s. 2020)
In addition to the positions previously created under Section 4 of Municipal Ordinance No. 13, Series of 2020, a partial reorganization of the personnel structure of the Municipal Government of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur is hereby effected, pursuant to Section 76 of Republic Act No. 7160, otherwise known as the "Local Government Code of 1991."
Accordingly, there is hereby created the Department of the Public Employment Service Office (PESO), with a corresponding plantilla position of Municipal Government Department Head I (PESO Manager), with a Salary Grade of 24, subject to existing civil service rules and regulations.
# SECTION 6. MINIMUM QUALIFICATION STANDARDS (Amending Section 5 of Ordinance No. 13 s. 2020)
Section 5 of Municipal Ordinance No. 13, Series of 2020, is hereby amended to include the following qualification standards, in accordance with the Civil Service Commission guidelines, for the position of Municipal Government Department Head I (PESO Manager):
| POSITION TITLE | EDUCATION | ELIGIBILITY | RELEVANT WORK EXPERIENCE | RELEVANT TRAINING |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Municipal Government Department Head I (PESO Manager) | Bachelor's degree preferable in any of the following: Operations Management (OM); Human Resource Management (HRM); Human Resource Development (HRD); and/or allied fields | Career Service Professional/2^{nd} Level Eligibility | 3 years of supervisory/management experience in program management relative to employment facilitation | None Required |
# SECTION 7. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF MUNICIPAL GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENT HEAD I (PESO MANAGER) (SG-24)
The PESO Manager shall be primarily responsible for the planning, supervision, coordination, and overall management of the Public Employment Service Office. Specifically, the PESO Manager shall:
a. Manage all technical and administrative operations of the PESO;
b. Formulate and implement action plans, project proposals, and other necessary documentation in support of PESO programs and services;
c. Assess and identify the training and development needs of staff and arrange appropriate interventions, whether in-house or through external providers;
d. Exercise supervision over PESO personnel, including responsibility for informal disciplinary procedures, coaching, and counseling;
and maintain an efficient process flow to enhance service delivery and minimize client complaints;
Conduct periodic reviews of office procedures and recommend improvements or corrective measures as necessary;
g. Maintain continuous communication with the Local Chief Executive (LCE) for policy alignment and program coordination; and
h. Perform such other duties and functions as may be assigned by the immediate supervisor and/or the Local Chief Executive.
Municipal Ordinance No. 05 | Page 3
## SECTION 8. BUDGETARY REQUIREMENTS
The funding requirements for the operation of the upgraded PESO Department, including salaries, benefits, and administrative costs for the newly created plantilla position, shall be included in the Annual Budget of the Municipality of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur, subject to the Personnel Services (PS) limitation provided under Republic Act No. 7160 and other applicable budgetary laws, rules, and regulations.
## SECTION 9. SEPARABILITY CLAUSE
If any provision or part of this Ordinance is declared invalid or unconstitutional, the remaining provisions unaffected thereby shall remain in full force and effect.
## SECTION 10. REPEALING CLAUSE
All prior ordinances, executive orders, resolutions, rules, or regulations inconsistent with any of the provisions of this Ordinance are hereby repealed, amended, or modified accordingly.
## SECTION 11. EFFECTIVITY CLAUSE
This Ordinance shall take effect immediately upon its approval.
**ENACTED**, this 25th day of June 2025, by a unanimous vote of all members of the Sangguniang Bayan during its 111th Regular Session.
