# ENACTING AN ORDINANCE ESTABLISHING THE SANTA CRUZ
MANPOWER TRAINING AND ASSESSMENT CENTER IN THE
MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, ESTABLISHING
GUIDELINES AND PROVIDING FUNDS THEREFOR
WHEREAS, Article XIV, Section 1 of the 1987 Philippine Constitution provides that the state shall protect and promote the right of all citizens to quality education at all levels, and shall take appropriate steps to make such education accessible to all;
WHEREAS, Republic Act No. 10533, otherwise known as the "Enhanced Basic Education Act of 2013," covers vocational and technical career opportunities as well as creative arts, sports and entrepreneurial employment;
WHEREAS, the integration of technical vocational education in the implementation of R.A 10533 has broadened the goals of basic education, as well as the role and participation of Technical-Vocational Institutions;
WHEREAS, the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur is cognizant of the need to upgrade the economic level of its constituents through skills development for the better employability of entrepreneurship;
WHEREAS, the LGU has consistently recognized the importance of providing its constituents with relevant training opportunities that align with industry demands;
WHEREAS, the establishment of Santa Cruz Manpower Training and Assessment Center will not only serve as a venue for skills training but also serve as an Income Generating Program of the Local Government thereby augmenting the income of the Local Government to expand its services for economic development;
WHEREAS, the Santa Cruz Manpower Training and Assessment Center will be operated by LGU-Santa Cruz in partnership with TESDA. This will enhance the workforce development strategies in the municipality, provide skill-based training programs, conduct assessments for various trades and act as a resource for both jobseekers and employers;
WHEREAS, Section of 458 (5) (x) of Republic Act No. 7160 otherwise known as the Local Government Code of 1991 provides that, "subject to the availability of funds and to existing laws, rules and regulations, establish and provide for operation of the vocational and technical schools and similar post-secondary institution and, with the approval of the Department of Education, Culture and Sports or the Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA), fix and collect reasonable fees and other school charges in educational institutions supported by the municipal government;
Municipal Ordinance No. 03, s. 2025 | Page 1
**WHEREAS**, series of committee hearings were conducted to discuss the provisions of the proposed ordinance and such has been referred to the Municipal Legal Officer for his comment and opinion. After the submission of the legal opinion, another committee hearing was conducted of which the discussion focused on the recommended amendments and the same has been considered and supported by the joint committees;
**WHEREFORE**, on motion of Hon. Roche S. Cabanda, duly seconded by Hon. Charlotte F. Gallego, it was
**RESOLVED**, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to enact the following:
# **MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 03**
Series of 2025
# **AN ORDINANCE ESTABLISHING THE SANTA CRUZ MANPOWER TRAINING AND ASSESSMENT CENTER IN THE MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR, ESTABLISHING GUIDELINES AND PROVIDING FUNDS THEREFOR**
**BE IT ORDAINED** by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, in session assembled, that:
**SECTION 1. TITLE.** This Ordinance shall be known as 'SANTA CRUZ MANPOWER TRAINING AND ASSESSMENT CENTER ORDINANCE IN THE MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR';
**SECTION 2. DECLARATION OF POLICY.** It is hereby declared the policy of the Municipality of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur to provide measures in reducing unemployment rate and promote technical skills in the local workforce through relevant and high quality technical education and skills development training.
The SANTA CRUZ MANPOWER TRAINING AND ASSESSMENT CENTER (hereinafter referred to as 'The Center') shall primarily provide technical-vocational education and training (TVET) Programs to students and local residents from low-income families and out-of-school youths, including persons with disabilities and indigenous peoples, in the Municipality of Santa Cruz and the neighboring localities in the Province of Davao del Sur, to help them become productive, self-reliant and globally competitive labor assets;
**SECTION 3. OBJECTIVES.** It affirms the commitment of the Local Government Unit (LGU) in the provision of technical education and skills development programs and complimentary support services for socio-economic upliftment of the constituents of the Municipality.
The LGU shall strengthen the development of skills through Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) Programs and shall foster Community-Based Training for enterprise development to capacitate the constituents for self-employment and entrepreneurship;
**SECTION 4. DEFINITION OF TERMS.** The following terms as used in this Ordinance shall mean:
**a). Certificate of Training** - is a certification issued by the LGU to trainees/students/scholars who have achieved the required number of hours for a qualification taken;
**b). Qualification** - shall refer to skills or competencies defined under the Philippine Technical Vocational Education and Training Qualification Framework (PTQF) of the Technical Educational Skills and Development Authority (TESDA);
**c). National Certificate (NC)** - is a certification issued to individuals who achieve all the required unit of competency for a national nullification defined under the training regulations. NCs are aligned to specific levels within the Philippine Technical Vocational
Municipal Ordinance No. 03, s. 2025 | Page 2
Education and Training Qualification Framework (PTQF) of the Technical Education Skills and Development Authority (TESDA);
d). National Certificate level/ Competency Certificate - refers to the qualification levels defined in the PTQF and, as used in this Ordinance, where the worker in:
1.) NC I performs a routine and predictable tasks, has little judgment, and works under supervision; and
2.) NC II performs prescribe range of functions involving known routines and procedures, has limited choice and complexity of functions, and has little accountability;
e). Persons with Disabilities (PWD)- refers to persons suffering restriction or different abilities, as a result of a mental, physical or sensory impairment, to perform an activity in a manner or within the range considered normal for human beings. Disability shall mean (1) a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits one more psychological, physiological or anatomical function of an individual or activities of such individuals; (2) a record of such an impairment; or (3) being regarded as having such an impairment;
f). Skilled Labor- refers to work that requires qualification in which a person uses judgment to determine the machine and manual operations in order to obtain the proper form, quality, or quantity of materials to be produced. Skilled work may require laying out work estimating quality, determining the suitability and needed quantities of materials, making precise measurements, reading blueprints or other specification, or making necessary computations or mechanical adjustments to control or regulate the work;
g). Skill - shall mean the acquired and practiced ability to carry out task or job;
h). Skills Development - shall mean the process through which learners and workers are systematically provided with learning opportunities to acquire or upgrade, or both, their ability, knowledge and behavior pattern required as qualifications for a job range of jobs in a given occupational are;
i). Technical Education - refers to skills competency training designed by the Technical Education Skills and Development Authority;
j). Trainers - shall mean persons who direct the practice of skills towards immediate improvement in some tasks;
k). Trainer's trainers - shall mean persons who provide training of trainers aimed at developing the latter's capacities for imparting attitudes, knowledge, skills, and behavior patterns required for specific jobs, tasks, occupations, or group of related occupations;
I). Trainees/Grantees/Scholars/Students - shall mean persons who are participants in a vocational and training program for the purpose acquiring and developing job related skills;
m). Training cum Production- refers to a program or initiative designed to provide individuals with both training in specific skills or qualification and producing goods and services related to the training;
n). Unskilled Labor - refers to work, which needs little or no judgment that can be learned on the job in a short period of time. The job may or may not require considerable strength;
SECTION 5. CREATION OF MUNICIPAL TECHNICAL EDUCATION AND SKILLS DEVELOPMENT COUNCIL (MTESDC). Upon the effectively of this Ordinance, the Local Chief Executive shall issue an Executive Order creating the MTESDC prescribing the composition, roles and functions and operational log frame;
SECTION 6. ROLE OF THE TESDA. The Technical Education Skills and Development Authority through the MTESDC shall assist the LGU by administering the following:
Municipal Ordinance No. 03, s. 2025 | Page 3
a) Assist in the registration of Skills Training Program conducted through the Community-Based Technical Vocational Education Training;
b) Provide technical assistance in the registration of Center-based program;
c) Provide Competency Certificate to the trainers/ instructors who will carry out the lectures and actual skills training;
d) Facilitate the conduct of capacity-building program to the personnel of the training center through trainer's training, skills upgrading and the other support mechanisms subject to the availability of funds and TESDA trainers;
e) Monitor the implementation of the training program on a quarterly basis;
f) Ensure the compliance of the Program to the TESDA systems and standards thru accreditation of the qualification integrated in the Program;
g) Issue certificate of training to qualified trainees who have accomplished the prescribed requirements of the qualification taken;
h) Facilitate the conduct of national competency assessment to the graduates of the Center; and
i) Provide scholarship allocation to the training center subject programs and provisions of the omnibus guidelines for TESDA scholarship program and availability of funds, and proper government accounting and auditing rules;
# SECTION 7. ROLE OF THE LGU. The LGU shall undertake the following:
a) Establish a training center that will serve as the venue for the conduct of various technical-vocational education and training program (TVET) undertakings;
b) Designate personnel who will run and manage the training center;
c) Register center-based TVET programs that are aligned with the identified skills priorities of the municipality;
d) Provide the facilities, tools, equipment and other supplies and materials needed in the establishment of the municipality;
e) Institutionalize the fund allocation for TEVET in local development plans of the Annual Investment Plan;
f) Provide assistance and information to TESDA in the identification of industry skills priorities, training need and other related researches; and
g) Participate in such other TVET programs as may be deemed necessary within its capabilities;
SECTION 8. COURSES OFFERED. In keeping with the network demand and priority, the Center shall offer technical-vocational courses attuned to the needs and demands of the constituents;
SECTION 9. QUALIFICATIONS OF TRAINEES/ GRANTEES/SCHOLARS. Trainees, grantees and scholars of technical vocational education training must possess the following qualifications:
a) Must be a bonafide resident of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur; and
b) Must be at least 15 years of age, without regard to trainee's gender or sex.
Prospective students shall undergo an interview and shall attend an orientation before the start of classes;
SECTION 10. PRIORITIZATION OF TRAINEES/GRANTEES/SCHOLARS. Priority shall be given to the following applicants:
a) Those whose family income fall below the poverty threshold based on the data from the Municipal Social and Welfare Development
b) Those who are not graduates of any four (4)- year course;
c) Those who are married or heads of the family;
d) Those who are considered as Persons with Disabilities (PWD);
e) Those who are solo parents;
f) Those who are member of Indigenous Groups;
g) Out-of-School Youths; and
h) An Alternative Learning System (ALS) passer (Secondary Level);
