SECTION 20. Artificial Reefs and Other Fish Aggregating Devices (FAD). The construction, installation and deployment of artificial reefs and other fish aggregating devices or payao in the municipal waters shall be subject to existing laws, rules and regulations, and shall not unduly affect the sustained productivity nor decrease the biodiversity of the natural environment through their use or misuse. Provided, however, that before the artificial reefs and other fish aggregating devices or payao are installed and/or constructed in the municipal waters, there should be an assessment of the proposed site, monitoring programs and management plans. Provided, further, that artificial reefs and other fish aggregating devices or payao shall not be placed within at least five (5) kilometers away from fish sanctuaries; one and a half (1.5) kilometers from the coral reef areas.
SECTION 21. Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) System. All proposed projects and undertaking by agencies and institutions of the government, including government-owned and controlled corporations, as well as private corporations, firms and entities which may significantly affect the quality of the environment shall be guided by the Environmental Impact Statement (EIS) System. The preparation of the EIS shall form an integral part of the entire planning process. No person, natural or judicial, shall undertake any development project without first securing Environmental Compliance Certificate (ECC) from the concerned agency of the government as provided by law.
