SECTION 23. Protection of Rare, Threatened and Endangered Species. The municipal government shall take conservation and rehabilitation measures to protect threatened or endangered species as may be determined by agencies concerned, and shall prohibit fishing and taking of rare, threatened or endangered species, including their eggs and young and reproducing individuals as identified by existing national and international laws.
SECTION 24. Closed Season. In order to allow the species to regenerate their population, no Commercial Fishing is allowed to take and catch any small pelagic species from June 01 to August 31 of every year in Davao Gulf (DILG JAO no.02: Establishing a Closed Season for the Conservation of Small Pelagic Species). It shall be unlawful for any person, association, or corporation to catch, or caught or taken, any small pelagic in the conservation area using ringnet and bagnet regardless of tonnage and/ or modified fishing gears with similar fishing operations. Likewise, the use of fine mesh net for the ringnet and bagnet and similar fishing gears or operation throughout the years is prohibited.
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 15
24.1. Designation of Closed Season in the Catching and Gathering of Siganid, locally known as Danggit. The municipal government in consultation with the MFARMC shall designate close season in the catching and gathering of Siganid, locally known as danggit that spawns during the period of four (4) days before new moon and seven (7) days after new moon or the total of eleven (11) days for the month of March, April, May and June respectively.
24.2. Financial Assistance To The Closed Season Affected Fisherfolks. The municipal government shall allocate budget for the financial assistance to the affected fisherfolk during the implementation of closed season.
SECTION 25. Mangrove Protection and Conservation. The municipal government Environment and Natural Resources Management Division (ENRMD), in coordination with the Department of Environment and Natural Resources, the FARMC's and other concerned organization, shall initiate proper management of mangrove areas. Provided, that the municipal government, in coordination with the Department of Environment and Natural Resources shall develop programs that promote and ensure community participation in the rehabilitation and management of existing mangrove areas. Provided further, that all developed programs shall conform to the provision of Section 99 of RA 10654.
SECTION 26. Regulation of Ornamental Fishes/Aquarium Aquatic Life Industry. No person, corporation, partnership or association shall sell, trade and distribute ornamental fishes/ aquarium aquatic life without securing a business permit in the municipality.
An auxiliary invoice shall be issued to a person, corporation, partnership or association after the inspection prior to transport. Collecting endangered or vulnerable species cited in CITES shall not be allowed, and any person in position for any endangered and vulnerable species shall be penalized according to law.
SECTION 27. Protection of Bangus Breeding Ground. The municipal government, in consultation with the FARMC, shall regulate the construction and installation of any structure 1 km from the shore waters, river mouths, and mangrove areas. During the breeding season, adult milkfish occur in small to large schools near the coasts or around islands where reefs are well developed. The eggs and larvae are pelagic up to 2-3 weeks. Milkfish larvae migrate towards the coast and the 10-17 mm postlarvae (known as 'fry' in the industry) reach shore waters where they are collected in large numbers and used as seed in the grow-out industry.
SECTION 28. Protection of Other Marine Habitats. The municipal government, in coordination with the FARMC and other concerned organizations shall ensure the protection and conservation of other marine habitats in the municipal waters. Provided, that the municipal government, in consultation with the FARMC, shall regulate the use of fishing gears and other human activities that may adversely affect the marine habitat.
SECTION 29. Coastal Air and Aquatic Pollution. All activities in the grounds or waters, directly or indirectly, which result or likely to result in such deleterious effect which harm living and non-living aquatic resources, hazards to human health, hindrance to coastal or fishery activities such as fishing and navigation, including dumping and disposal of waste and other marine litter shall be prohibited; Provided, that it shall be the responsibility of the polluter to contain, remove and clean-up pollutants at his/her own expense; Provided, however, that in case of failure to do so, the municipal government in coordination with other concerned agencies and institutions, shall undertake containment, removal and clean-up operations and the expenses incurred in said operation shall be charged against the person and/or entities responsible for such pollution.
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 16
SECTION 30. Maintenance of Water Quality and Cleanliness. The municipal government shall monitor the quality of the water at the optimal level relative to natural productivity and the cleanliness of the areas devoted for aquaculture development.
Critical parameter :
a.) Dissolved Oxygen (D.O.) of at least level 5.0 mg/ltr.
b.) Desired Ph at least 6.5 TO 9
c.) NH3 (toxic ammonia) not more than 1.0 mg/ltr
The operators and owners of aquaculture facilities shall develop a mechanism of proper waste disposal. Violation of this section may be ground for the cancellation of the permit to operate aquaculture activities.
SECTION 31. Use of Fish Shelter (Payao). The municipal government shall regulate the use of existing payao and other fish aggregating devices in the municipal water; Provided, that only registered municipal fishers shall utilize the existing payao in the municipal waters.
SECTION 32. Navigational Route. The municipal government in consultation with the FARMC, shall designate the navigational route of ferries and other fishing crafts and shall disallow any activity that shall obstruct the designated navigational route: Provided, That nothing in the foregoing section shall be construed as permitting the lease, licensee or permittee to undertake any construction which may obstruct free navigation and impede water circulation such as the flow of tide to and from the area.
