SECTION 37. Fish Coral. The municipal government, in consultation with the MFARMC, shall regulate the construction and operation of fish corrals in the municipal waters: Provided, that no fish corral shall be established and operated outside of the designated areas for the establishment and operation of fish corral: Provided however, that no fish corral shall be constructed within one hundred (100) meters any part thereof from another fish corral; one (1) km from the fish sanctuaries buffer zone: Provided further, that the tail of the fish corral shall not be more than 100 meters and should not block the navigational zone; Provided furthermore, that the mesh size of the net of the fish corral shall not be less than 3 centimeters and shall be entirely lifted during the designated closed season of gathering of danggit, to enable a considerable number of spawner/breeder to reach their spawning ground: Provided, Finally, that ownership of fish corral shall be limited to only one per permittee. The interested parties who wish to construct and operate fish corrals in the zones stated in this Section shall secure individual license from the Office of the Mayor upon payment of the necessary permit fee. Provided, further, that fish corral shall not use fine mesh net in their operation.
SECTION 38. Regulation of Modified Baby Ring Net (Likos- Pangbolinao/ Pangturnos). The municipal government shall regulate the use and operation of Modified Baby Ringnet. After the approval of this ordinance, the Local Chief Executive and the MAGRO, in consultation with the MFARMC, shall create guidelines in the registration for new gear application of modified baby ringnet. The MAGRO- Fishery Management Section shall be furnished the list of existing operators upon the approval of this ordinance.
The operation of Modified Baby ringnet (Likos- Pangbolinao) shall be allowed within five (5) days on its season, which is to be determined by the Municipal Agriculture Office- Fishery Management Section. The allowable period shall be subject to extension duly certified by the Municipal Agriculture Office- Fishery Management Section.
In all instances the operation of Modified Baby ringnet (Likos- Pangbolinao) shall be allowed in the following catch composition: Tornos, Bolinao, and Hipon.
SECTION 39. Regulation of Modified Baby Ring Net (Likos). The municipal government shall regulate the use and operation of Modified Baby Ringnet. After the approval of this ordinance, the Local Chief Executive and the MAGRO, in consultation with the MFARMC, shall create guidelines in the registration for new gear application for modified baby ringnet. The MAGRO- Fishery Management Section shall have the list of existing operators before the approval of this ordinance.
The operation of Modified Baby ringnet shall be allow only in 10.1-15 kilometers area of municipal waters.
