SECTION 46. Registry of Fishing Banca. Adopting EO No. 305 Series Of 2005 Entitled "Devolving To Municipal And City Governments The Registration Of Fishing Vessel Three (3) Gross Tonnage (And) Below", And Imposing Fees Thereto.
All fishing bancas operating and/or fishing within the municipal waters must be registered annually. Only registered fishing bancas shall be allowed to fish and/or operate within the municipal waters.
An inventory of registered fishing bancas shall be maintained, and from time to time updated, by the Office of the Municipal Agriculturist and be made available for public inspection.
46.a. Requirements for Registration of a Fishing Banca. The following shall be required for the registration of fishing banca:
1. Duly accomplished registration form;
2. Certification from the Philippine National Police (clearance from PNP Maritime Office in the LGU or in an absence, local PNP) certifying that the fishing vessel is not involved in any criminal offense (0.30 GT non-motorized banca is excluded);
3. Barangay Certification of ownership;
4. Invoice/receipt of engine (new), if applicable;
5. Deed of Sale/Affidavit of Ownership, if second hand;
6. Colored picture of owner along with the fishing boat to be registered;
7. Latest colored 2x2 picture of owner; and
8. Payment fees.
46.b. Permit to Operate. Registered fishing bancas shall only be operated by person with a permit to operate from the municipality. In the absence of a Boat Captain License, the following natural persons may apply for a permit to operate a fishing banca 3 gross tons and below:
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 20
1. If a single proprietorship:
a. The duly registered owner of the fishing banca;
b. The spouse of the registered owner;
c. An emancipated child by consanguinity or affinity of the registered owner;
2. If a partnership, any of the above person related to either partner;
The use of the Permit to Operate shall be limited to the registered fishing banca of the immediate family member only to the exclusion of other registered fishing bancas in the municipality. The Permit to Operate shall be co-terminus to the validity of the registration of the fishing banca.
Other person who wishes to operate fishing bancas neither owned by nor registered to them or their immediate family, or is owned or registered to a corporation or a cooperative, must be a registered fisherfolk certified by the Municipal Agriculturist.
46.c. Requirements for Issuance of Permit to Operate. The following requirements must be complied for issuance of permit to operate:
1. Certificate of registration of fishing banca
2. If not the registered owner, any proof of relationship (Marriage Contract, Birth Certificate, Barangay Certification)
3. Duly accomplished application form
4. Copy of previous permit to operate (for renewal)
5. Boat Captain license issued by the MARINA (if other person not mentioned in Section 8, (no. 2) wish to operate
6. Payment of Fees
46.d. General Registration Guidelines.
1. Application - The applicant has to file his/her application using the prescribed application form, which shall contain the following information: name of owner, nationality, residence, type and make of fishing banca and propulsion, and other pertinent information that the Municipality Government may require.
2. Qualification - Only Filipino citizens, single proprietorships, partnership and/or corporation and duly registered or accredited fisherfolk associations and cooperatives that are residents of the Municipality of Santa Cruz, Davao del Sur are eligible to apply for registration.
3. Tonnage Measurement - The Municipality Government with the assistance of MARINA shall train and authorize a pool of inspectors to conduct inspection of the fishing banca to determine its gross tonnage using the metric formula as follows:
Gross Tonnage = Tonnage Length x Tonnage Breadth x Tonnage Depth x 0.70
2.83
The inspector shall certify the correctness of the admeasurements in the standard tonnage measurement form.
Should the inspector find out that the banca is not a fishing banca or if it is but exceeds a gross tons, he shall recommend that the application be endorsed to the MARINA for appropriate registration.
4. Issuance of a Certificate of Number and Permit to Operate - After evaluation of application and the inspection of vessel and everything is found to be in order, the applicant shall be issued a certificate of number and the corresponding Permit to Operate, if applicable
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 21
# 5. Official Number, Assignment of Name and Marking of Fishing Banca
a. Official Number – The Municipal Government shall use the series DAS-09-0001 as official number to a registered fishing banca, which shall be permanently marked on the both sides of the forward portion of the banca, each letter / number are to be painted GOLD in color and must contrast with its background. The codes shall have a dimension of at least three-inch-high bold BLOCK letters/numbers.
b. Assignment of Name – A fishing banca shall be assigned a name. A name shall be assigned to only one (1) fishing banca regardless of type of fishing gear. If the proposed name has already been assigned to another registered boat, the owner or operator has the option of adding letters of the alphabet, any Arabic number or roman numeral, which can be represented by word or its numeric equivalent, to the proposed name. The name of the banca shall be of the same color and dimension as of the code and shall be painted on both sides of the mid portion thereof.
46.e. Monitoring of Registered Banca. The Municipal Government shall institute a monitoring system to determine compliance with this ordinance.
46.f. Re-issuance of Certificate of Number. A certificate of number shall be re-issued by the Municipal Government, retaining the official number, in the following instance:
1. Change in Ownership. In case the fishing banca is the subject of sale or transfer of ownership the Municipal Government shall re-issue the certificate of number, containing the amended information on ownership upon application of the owner or transferee, and subject to compliance with the following requirements:
a. Duly notarized Deed of Absolute Sale;
b. Posting in the Barangay or Municipal Hall for 5 consecutive days giving notice that the fishing banca has been sold or transferred to a new owner;
c. Affidavit of Publication executed by the Barangay Captain and BFARMC that said notice has been posted in the premises and that there are no oppositors to the motorized fishing banca sale; and,
d. Original copy of the certificate of registration.
2. Change of Technical Specification. A change in the technical specifications of the banca is any change that would alter its size or engine specifications. An application for the re-issuance of the certification of number shall be filled accompanied by the following:
a. Original copy of certificate of numbers;
b. Official Receipt of Purchase of engine and/or sketch plan showing the alteration/s; and
c. Police clearance from Traffic Management Group (TMG) that the engine purchased is not from a car napped/stolen vehicle.
3. Change of name of the fishing banca. The Municipal Government shall re-issue a certificate of number when an owner or operator desires to change the name of his fishing banca, upon application stating the reason for such. An application for change of name will not be approved if the fishing banca is involved in civil case regarding question of ownership or in a criminal case for violation of a fishery law or ordinance.
4. Loss of the Certificate of Number. A lost certificate of number may be re-issued upon application accompanied by the following documents:
a. Affidavit of Loss narrating the circumstances of the loss;
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 22
b. Posting of the application and affidavit in a conspicuous place in the municipal building and/or barangay hall for at least five consecutive days.
46.g. Issuance of a New Certificate of Number. Should there be application for a change in homeport to the municipality and a clearance for a change of homeport from the previous homeport was presented by the applicant; a new certificate of number shall be issued reflecting the new homeport.
46.h. Clearance for a Change in Homeport. A change in homeport may occur in case the owner/operator changes residence or principal office, or sells or transfers ownership of the fishing banca, to a person or entity with residency in another Municipality/City. The following rules shall be observed for the issuance of a clearance for a change in homeport:
1. The owner shall file an application for a clearance for a change in homeport with the municipality and pay the corresponding fees;
2. Such application shall be posted in a conspicuous place in the barangay hall building for at least five consecutive days;
3. If there is no opposition to the application, the municipal government shall thereafter issue a clearance for a change of homeport and shall delete the registration of such fishing banca from its registry;
4. Should there be an opposition to the application, the application shall be referred to the Lupon ng mga Barangay for appropriate action;
5. No clearance for a change of homeport shall be issued under the following instances:
a. The owner of the fishing banca has unpaid and outstanding fees with the municipal government;
b. There is an outstanding safety requirement, which the fishing banca has to comply;
c. The fishing banca is involved in a pending criminal or administrative case for violation of a fishery law or ordinance or a civil case regarding question of ownership.
46.i. Deletion/ Cancellation of Registration. Upon information of the owner/operator, the Municipality Government shall delete or cancel the registration of the fishing banca in the following instances:
1. Change of homeport to another municipality/city
2. In case of loss or decay of the fishing banca,
The Municipal Government may also cancel or delete the registration of the fishing banca for other lawful causes, after duly notifying its owner/operator and compliance with the requirements of due process.
46.j. Record-Keeping and Submission of Record. The Municipal Government shall maintain an update of fishing bancas and semi-annually submit to the Maritime Industry Authority (MARINA) Regional Office XI a list of fishing bancas registered and deleted/cancelled. The semi-annual reports shall be submitted on the last working days of the last month of the semester.
