SECTION 47. Monitoring, Control and Surveillance. The municipal government, in consultation with the MFARMC and other agencies and institutions, shall establish effective mechanisms and guidelines for monitoring, control and surveillance to ensure compliance with policies, programs and projects on conservation, protection and management of coastal and fishery resources. Provided, however, that the municipal government, in consultation with the MFARMC shall establish mechanisms and guidelines for water quality monitoring and surveillance. Provided, further, that such mechanisms and guidelines shall be subjected to periodic review by the municipal government, in consultation with the MFARMC.
