# ARTICLE XII
# FISHERIES AND AQUATIC RESOURCES MANAGEMENT COUNCIL
SECTION 54. Creation of Municipal Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Management Council (MFAMRC). Pursuant to Section 69 of the Philippine Fisheries Code of 1998, municipal FARMC shall be established in this municipality. The municipal government shall provide assistance to the Municipal FARMC.
SECTION 55. Composition of Municipal FARMC. The regular members of the Municipal FARMC shall be composed of the following:
a. Municipal Planning and Development Officer;
b. Chairperson of the Sangguniang Bayan Committee on Agriculture/ Fisheries;
c. Representative of the Municipal Development Council;
d. Municipal Environment and Natural Resources Management Officer;
e. Representative from the accredited non-government organization;
f. Representative on the private sector;
g. Representative from the Municipal Agriculture Office; and
h. At least eleven (11) fisher representatives, composed of seven (7) municipal fishers, one (1) fish worker and three (3) commercial fishers in each municipality which include representative from youth and women sector.
The FARMC shall adopt rules and regulations necessary to govern its proceedings and election.
SECTION 56. Powers and Function of the Municipal FARMC. The Municipal FARMC shall have the following powers and functions:
1. To assist the municipal government in the implementation of programs and projects on coastal and fisheries resources management;
2. To assist the municipal government in the monitoring and evaluation coastal and fisheries resources management programs;
3. To advise the municipal government in the arbitration of disputes over fishery rights and sharing contract;
4. To assist the municipal government in the conduct of public hearings and community consultations, in aid of the formulation of plans, policies and proposed ordinances and regulations;
5. To coordinate with law enforcement agencies in the enforcement of fishery and environmental laws, ordinances, rules and regulations;
6. To assist the municipal government in the promotion of comprehensive rehabilitation and conservation of municipal fishing grounds and coastal and fishery resources;
![img-11.jpeg](img-11.jpeg)
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 26
7. To assist the municipal government in the promotion of ancillary economic activities, including cooperation marketing and socio-economic services;
8. To maintain the updated registry of municipal fishers; and
9. To perform such other functions the Municipal Mayor, the Municipal Development Council and the Sangguniang Bayan may delegate, as provided by ordinance or resolution.
### ARTICLE XIII
CREATION OF ADDITIONAL PLANTILLA POSITIONS FOR FISHERY MANAGEMENT SECTION
SECTION 57. Title of Positions. There shall be creation of additional plantilla positions and salary grade for Fishery Management Section of Municipal Agriculture office for better management and law enforcement.
1. Aquaculturist I, Salary Grade 11
2. Special Agent II, Salary Grade 10
