## ARTICLE XIV
PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES AND PENALTIES
SECTION 60. Compliance with National Laws. All relevant national laws, orders, rules and regulations shall be implemented in this municipality.
SECTION 61. Other Prohibition. It shall be unlawful for any person, entities, organization or corporation to engage in the following activities:
a. Use of Compressor and Oxygen in Tanks in Spear Fishing;
b. Use of Nukos Ambak-ambak in Fishing/ Lambada (Fish Net with Scaring Device);
c. Use of Sudsod in Fishing (Man Push Net);
d. Use of Liba-liba in Fishing, regardless of Mesh Size (Danish Siene);
e. Beach Siene (Baling);
f. Use of Bagnet (Basnig) and Ringnet (Likom/ Sinsoro), Baby Ring Net (Kubkuban/ Likos) in Fishing in municipal waters is prohibited within 1-10 kilometers;
g. Use of Pakaras in Fishing (using rake for gleaning);
h. Use of Triple Nets in Fishing;
i. Use of Obnoxious and Poisonous Substance in Fishing (Dynamite);
j. Use of Trawl;
k. Use of Sangab (fry gatherer) shall be only used seasonally;
1. Use of Hoop Net;
m. Use of motorized push net (Sudsud);
n. Moro-ami (Drive in Net);
o. Superlight (500 watts and above);
p. To establish / operate any fishery activity without any approved permit/license from the municipal government.
SECTION 62. All Violators shall be punished with a fine of Two Thousand Five Hundred Pesos (Php 2,500.00) or an imprisonment of six (6) months, or both at the discretion of the court and the confiscation of the fishing paraphernalia.
## ARTICLE XV
FISHERY LAW ENFORCEMENT
SECTION 63. Responsible Office. The Office of the Municipal Mayor, through the MAGRO-Fisheries Management Section (FMS) is hereby authorized to organize Barangay Coast Watch (Fishery Law Enforcement Team) in each of the coastal barangays of this municipality.
SECTION 64. Creation of Municipal Bantay Dagat (Bantay Dagat of Santa Cruz) for Purposes of Fully Implementing and Enforcing all Laws, Rules and Regulations Relative to the Preservation, Conservation and Protection of Aquatic Life and Resources. There shall be at least two Barangay Coast Watch or Bantay Dagat representative per coastal barangay, who shall be duly deputized by the Local Chief Executive and trained by the BFAR.
The Bantay Dagat shall be responsible for the patrol and implementation and enforcement of fishery laws, rules and regulations.
Subject to availability of funds, the Bantay Dagat may receive an honorarium of Two Thousand Pesos (P 2,000.00) per month.
SECTION 65. Powers and Function. The fishery law enforcement teams are authorized to assist regular law enforcement officers such as the Philippine National Police Maritime Group, Philippine Coast Guard, or Philippine Navy, the local PNP, in the enforcement of
Comprehensive Municipal Fisheries Ordinance of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur | Page 28
the provisions of this Ordinance as well as all other laws, rules, and regulations on fisheries and aquatic resources. The fishery law enforcement teams shall also assist the FMS in carrying out its duties and function. For legal purposes, they are deemed to be person rendering assistance to person in authority, and shall be subject to the direct control and supervision of a regular law enforcement office.
**SECTION 66. Accreditation Necessary.** No person shall become a member of the fishery law enforcement teams unless he or she has successfully completed the training course in fishery law enforcement as prescribed by the Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources and has been duly deputized for those purposes.
## ARTICLE XVI
GENERAL PROVISION
**SECTION 67. Persons and Deputies Authorized to Enforce this Ordinance.** The Municipal Mayor, Municipal Agriculturist, Municipal Planning and Coordinator, Municipal Treasurer, Municipal Local Government Operation Officer, Philippine National Police, Municipal FARMC, Barangay Officials and Deputize fish warden shall take lead in the implementation of this ordinance.
**SECTION 68. Mandatory Review.** The Sangguniang Bayan shall undertake the mandatory review of this ordinance at least once every 3 years and as often as it may deem necessary, to ensure that coastal and fisheries policies and guidelines remain responsive to the changing circumstances.
## ARTICLE XVII
FINAL PROVISIONS
**SECTION 69. Appropriation.** The sum necessary to effectively carry out the provisions of this ordinance during the first year of its implementation shall be allocated from the budget of the Municipality.
**SECTION 70. Repealing Clause.** All previous ordinances, resolutions, executive order, rules and regulations or parts thereof and including barangay fishery ordinances approved by this body, which are inconsistent with this ordinance are hereby repealed and modified accordingly.
**SECTION 71. Separability Clause.** If, for any reason or reasons, any part or provision of this ordinance shall be held unconstitutional or invalid, other parts or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall continue to be in full force and in effect.
**SECTION 72. Effectivity Clause.** This Code shall take effect immediately after completion its publication.
**ENACTED**, this 16th day of October 2024, by a unanimous vote of all members of the Sangguniang Bayan present during its 90th Regular Session.
