# **ENACTING AN ORDINANCE SETTING GUIDELINES FOR THE OPERATION AND
MANAGEMENT OF THE WATERWORKS SYSTEM OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR TO BE
KNOWN AS THE 'WATERWORKS CODE OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR'**
**WHEREAS**, Section 17, Basic Services and Facilities, of RA 7160 otherwise known as the Local Government Code of 1991 provides that, “Local government units shall endeavor to be self-reliant and shall continue exercising the powers and discharging the duties and functions currently vested upon them. They shall also discharge the functions and responsibilities of national agencies and offices devolved to them pursuant to this Code. Local government units shall exercise such other powers and discharge such other functions and responsibilities as are necessary, appropriate or incidental to efficient and effective provision of the basic services and facilities;
**WHEREAS**, the Local Government Unit of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur has a strong commitment to ensure equitable, universal access to safe water and sanitation to protect the health, safety and welfare of its residents;
**WHEREAS**, access to water and sanitation are basic human rights recognized by the United Nations which has declared the right of every person to sufficient, safe, acceptable, accessible and affordable water;
**WHEREAS**, the LGU-Sta. Cruz thru the Local Economic Entertainment Management Office shall be responsible for the management, maintenance and operation of the waterworks system of the municipality;
**WHEREAS**, to ensure efficient operation and management of the waterworks system, guidelines should be set;
**WHEREFORE**, on motion of Hon. Apolinar C. Ugdoracion, Jr., unanimously seconded, it was
**RESOLVED**, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to enact the following:
# **MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 06**
Series of 2022
# **AN ORDINANCE ENACTING THE WATERWORKS CODE OF THE
MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR**
Be it ordained by the Sangguniang Bayan of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del sur, Davao del Sur in session assembled that:
# **ARTICLE I
TITLE**
This Ordinance shall be known and referred to as the “Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur”
*Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 1*
## ARTICLE II
DATE OF EFFECTIVITY
This Code shall take effect ten (10) days after its posting at the conspicuous places or publication.
## ARTICLE III
SCOPE AND COVERAGE
The Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur shall cover the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System which serves as one of the viable economic enterprises of the Municipality that will be under the Local Economic Enterprises Management Office.
## ARTICLE IV
BASIC POLICIES
It is the policy of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur to:
1. Recognize and uphold the basic principle that water resources of the Municipality are the natural wealth and patrimony of the constituents;
2. Protect and manage these resources for the use, enjoyment and benefit of the present and future generations;
3. Institute all measures necessary for conservation and protection of the water resources including its watershed areas;
4. Provide regulations on the manner of use or extraction and the prevention on depletion of the water resource through water protection.
## ARTICLE V
DEFINITION OF TERMS
Section 1 – Definition of Terms. As used in this Code, the following terms shall mean as herein stated:
1. **Alteration** – refers to a change either in the consumer's record or on his water line or a change to both of the same
2. **Bacteriological test** – Test used to determine if water is practically safe for human consumption
3. **Chlorination** – is the process of introducing chlorine into the water system in order to kill water borne diseases making it safe for human consumption
4. **Commodity Charge** – the charge per cubic meter of water consumed in excess of the minimum rate
5. **Consumer** – one who in accordance with this Ordinance has obtained a water service connection
6. **Cost** – Labor, materials, transportation, supervision, engineering and all other necessary overhead expenses
7. **Cross connection** – is an act where a person, firm or corporation shall install or maintain physical connection from a private source of water supply through the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System
8. **Disconnection Date** – the period after fifteen (15) days where Red Bill is serve to consumer
9. **Disconnection Job Order** – disconnection of water service line after the seven (7) days from the disconnection date
10. **Discount** – a proportionate amount deducted from the water bill for Senior Citizens and Persons With Disability (PWD)
11. **Due Date** – the last day of payment period without penalty
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 2
12. Illegal Tapping—an act of tapping the water service line connection without securing the necessary requirements from the Operation of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System
13. Minimum Rate - the base rate charge to the consumer for the first ten (10) cubic meters
14. Reconnection - a resumption of water supply to consumer whose water service line was temporarily disconnected
15. Service Cock - is a valve on the inlet side of the meter
16. Service Connection - a connection tapped from the water supply lines consisting of pipes, water ports, fittings and setting of water meter
17. Service Connection Fee - the cost of installing the consumer's water meter
18. Service Provider - refers to the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System
19. Surcharge - an additional ten (10) percent penalty base on the total bill due to non-payment of water bill after due date
20. Temporary Disconnection- the temporary closing of service cock/gate valve due to non-payment of water bill after Disconnection Notice
21. Water Bill - a statement of fees or charges on the sales or value of water consumed
22. Water Rate - the cost or value of water
23. Waterworks System - a water system that includes reservoir, tanks, buildings, pumps pipes, sedimentation, filtration and other appurtenances
24. Watershed - an area of land that contains a common set of streams and rivers that all drain into a single larger body of water.
# ARTICLE VI
MANAGEMENT AND SUPERVISION
# Section 2. STA. CRUZ WATERWORKS MANAGEMENT BOARD
There shall be created a Sta. Cruz Waterworks Management Board to be composed of the following:
| Chairperson | - Municipal Mayor |
| --- | --- |
| Vice Chairperson | - SB Chair on Economic Enterprise |
| Members | - SB Chair on Infrastructure & Utilities |
| | - Municipal Administrator |
| | - Local Economic Enterprise Manager |
| | - Environment and Natural Resources Officer |
| | - Municipal Health Officer |
| | - Municipal Engineer |
| | - Representative from the Private Sector |
| Secretariat | - Administrative staff: Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System |
# Section 3. Powers and Functions
1. Recommend policies to the Sangguniang Bayan regarding water resource protection, conservation, utilization, operation and management;
2. Prepare comprehensive plans and programs that will provide guidelines for the protection, conservation, utilization of water resources and likewise the operation and management of the waterworks system;
3. Coordinate with the national agencies or offices on activities related to water protection, conservation, utilization and development of water resources;
4. Direct the conduct of continuing education program to generate public awareness and support for the need of protecting, conserving the water resources of the Municipality.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 3
Section 4. Meeting – The Board shall meet once in every quarter however, the Chairperson may call a special meeting as the need arises.
Section 5. Honorarium – An honorarium maybe provided and will be determined by the Board subject to the usual accounting rules and regulations.
# Section 6. Manpower and Personnel Requirement
There is hereby created additional staff/personnel to man the Operation of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System and this will be headed by the Waterworks Superintendent who will take charge on the day to day operation and maintenance of the facility.
The administrative staff shall take charge on the accounts of consumers, billing and collections and other administrative works while the Operation and Maintenance staff will handle on the service line connections and maintenance of the facilities.
In the event that no additional employees are yet to be hired, the Local Chief Executive may designate regular employees to perform the functions and man the Operation of the Waterworks System. He may also engage on hiring employees through Contract of Services and/or Job Order Appointment.
