# ARTICLE VII
POLICIES ON THE OPERATION, CUSTOMER SRVICE AND MAINTENANCE
Section 8. Classification of Water Consumers - Water consumers shall be classified in the following manner as follows:
1. Commercial - Consumers under this classification are those drawing water from the system for the purpose of using the water directly or indirectly to promote their trade or occupation or to produce a commercial or saleable product.
2. Industrial - Business establishments or persons utilizing water for manufacturing process and other similar operations.
3. Institutional - Schools, churches, offices and banking institutions shall be under this classification
4. Residential/Domestic - Persons drawing water from the water utility and using it in pursuit of their day to day living such as cooking, washing, bathing, drinking, lawn/plants watering and other domestic use.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 7
# Section 9. One Meter, One Household Policy
Every consumer's dwelling within the service area shall be provided with only one (1) meter.
# Section 10. Application for Water Service Connection
Any person or establishment with the intent to apply for water service connection shall comply with the following requirements:
1. Applicants shall secure an application form from the Operation of the Waterworks System. He is required to fill up the forms and must abide the rules and regulations governing service connection as embodied therein;
2. The applicant shall attend the orientation seminar regarding the policies, rules and regulations as provided in the Ordinance pertaining the service connection which shall be conducted by the staff of the Operation of the Waterworks System at a scheduled date and time with identified specific place/venue.
3. Prior to the approval of the application, the Plumber Foreman shall conduct inspection on the availability of water supply on the area and the materials needed for the connection.
4. Upon approval, the applicant shall sign a Water Service Connection Contract stipulating therein all the terms and conditions pertaining to water service connection and upon presentation of official receipt of payments of all fees and charges.
# Section 11. Authority of the Local Chief Executive to enter into a Service Contract.
The Local Chief Executive is hereby granted an authority to enter into a Water Service Connection Contract with the Consumer relative to the water service connection.
# Section 12. Water Service Connection Contract (Contract Form)
The content of the Water Service Contract shall be read as follows:
This Contract made and entered into this ____ day of ____, 20 ____ at Sta. Cruz, Davao del sur, Philippines by and between the Local Government Unit (LGU) of Sta. Cruz, Davao del sur represented by the Local Chief Executive referred to as Service Provider and ____ with resident at ____, ta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, referred to as the Consumer;
The parties agree on the following terms and conditions as stipulated herein:
1. The Applicant -Consumer shall conform to the policies, regulations and guidelines set by the service Provider and all related laws and issuance pertaining to the operation of the water system;
2. The Applicant will pay the application fee and one month non-interest bearing guarantee deposit;
3. The Applicant-Consumer will, when water becomes available, purchase the water meter and water needs from the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System and will pay therefore the monthly rates, however, applicant agrees that the connection will not be made until all charges are paid and application is accepted and approved;
4. The Applicant-Consumer shall ensure the right location (outside the property line) of the water meter that shall be accessible to the Service Provider or its Authorized Representatives for meter reading and inspection.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 8
Further, the Applicant will grant to the Service Provider the necessary rights and easement to construct, operate, replace, repair and perpetually maintain on the property owned by the Applicant, its lines of pipes for the distribution of water and will execute and deliver instrument which the Service Provider shall consider necessary for the purpose. All pipes, or equipment installed by the Service Provider on the property of the Applicant shall be the sole property of the Municipal Government giving the latter the right of access to the property of the applicant to operate, maintain, repair or relocate, on this regard, the applicant is accountable for the water meter.
5. The Consumer shall be responsible in the maintenance of pipes and fixtures after the water meter going to their household while the Service Provider shall provide for the maintenance of materials before the water meter going to the water source. Water that passes through the meter reader whether consumed or wasted shall be the accountability of the Consumer;
6. The Applicant-Consumer shall be held responsible in protecting the water meter installed at the premises. In case the water meter shall be stolen or damaged, the Consumer shall be responsible for the replacement of the water meter upon payment of the unit from the Municipal Treasurer's Office.
7. The Applicant-Consumer shall pay the bills regularly and on time at the of the Municipal Treasurer's Office or its Authorized Representative;
8. A surcharge of ten (10) percent shall likewise be collected from the Consumer for failure to pay the bills and is considered delinquent. A Notice of Disconnection shall be served to the Customer for failure to settle his monthly obligation on the date stated. Disconnection of the water service connection shall be done without further notice if payment shall not be received within the grace period from receipt of the Notice of Disconnection. For reconnection, the Consumer shall pay the reconnection fee of ONE HUNDRED PESOS and full payment of the outstanding obligations;
9. Payment in lump sum shall be applied first to bills in arrears, surcharges and penalties before application to current obligations;
10. Should any meter becomes defective for one reason or another, the average consumption of the Consumer for six (6) months period previous to the date when the meter become defective shall be the basis for the computation of the subsequent bills;
11. The Service Provider shall not be held responsible on interruption of water service for causes beyond its control;
12. The Applicant-Consumer will not allow any person, firm or corporation from vending, selling or otherwise and disposing of water for public purposes within the service area without permission of the Service Provider where time or fix term and conditions by permit for such sale or disposition of water;
13. Illegal tapping, tampering of water meters, using jumpers or devices whereby water is stolen, pilfering of water or water meter shall be strictly prohibited and shall be sufficient ground for water disconnection and termination of this Contract without prejudice to criminal and/or civil action;
14. The Consumer shall make no changes in his/her approved connection without previously signing a revision of Contract for that purpose in the Local Economic Enterprise Management Office through the Operation of the sta. Cruz Water works System. The Consumer shall notify the Operation of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System in case of transfer of ownership or when the tenant leaves the premises;
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 9
15. In the event, that the consumer is only a tenant or does not own the house, the owner of the house or building shall be jointly and severally liable with the Consumer;
16. In the event of misrepresentation by the Applicant which has a new application and was discovered to have an old account, the Service Provider reserves the right to disconnect the new connection until full payment of the old account has been settled;
17. This Contract shall be subject for cancellation if the Consumer failed to pay the water bill within the grace period after the disconnection notice has been served.
