# Section 13. Water Service Connection
1. Size and Location - The Service Provider reserves the right to determine the size of service connections and their locations with respect to the boundaries of the premises to be served. The laying of consumers service lateral to the meter shall not be done until the location of the water services connection has been approved by the Waterworks Superintendent of the Operation Sta.. Cruz Waterworks System or its authorized representative.
2. Service Cock - Every water service connection installed by the Service Provider shall be equipped with a service cock or valve on the inlet side of the meter, which valve or service cock shall be for the exclusive use through the service lateral.
It is further provided that the service cock installed by the Service Provider shall not be used by the consumer for the purposes of shutting off the water supply. Consumer shall provide their own shut off valve and check the valve installed after the meter.
3. Water Meter – The water meter becomes the property of the LGU after payment of the cost at the Municipal Treasurer’s Office or its Authorized Representative. It shall be the responsibility of the Consumer to protect the water meter from any physical damages. In case of damage or stolen water meter, the Consumer shall also be responsible for its replacement.
Location of the water meter shall be outside the premises of the consumer.
All water connections shall be metered and no water services shall be delivered without payment of service fees and charges except for firefighting purposes specifically government installed hydrant.
The Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System reserves the right to set and maintain a meter on any connection.
4. Transfer of Name of Accounts. There will be transfer of account’s name when the transferee resides in the household of the previous consumer or the transferee takes possession of the property.
The consumer shall make a formal request letter to the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System specifying the reason of transfer provided that all obligations are settled.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 10
If formal letter is not secured due to the absence of previous consumer by whatsoever reason, the transferee shall make formal letter requesting for the transfer of account's name in his favor. He shall execute a duly notarized affidavit that consumer cannot be ascertained as to his availability.
In case of death of the registered consumer, any direct family member may apply for the transfer of account's name. The transferee shall present the death certificate of the registered consumer. The applicant will also attend the orientation seminar and sign all pertinent documents including the execution of new water service connection contract. Transfer fee shall be paid prior to the transfer of account's name by preceding reasons except by death.
When the account's name be transferred to a Senior Citizen, the latter will reapply and pay all the necessary fees, charges and settle previous accounts/obligations.
Any person or entity who shall take ownership or custody of household or office area with unpaid accounts before new connection shall comply with the regulations set by the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System and its Ordinance.
5. Red Bill. Non-payment of at least two (2) consecutive months on water consumption bills shall be a ground for disconnection and/ or cut-off water services.
Failure of the consumer to pay his/her delinquent bills within fifteen (15) days after receipt of the Red Bill, a Disconnection Notice will be served and the account will already bear a ten (10) percent penalty.
If no payments will be made within seven (7) days after the Disconnection Notice, Disconnection Job Order will be served and the disconnection of water service will be done by the personnel from the Operation of Sta. Cruz Water Works System without demand and prior notice to the Consumer.
6. Disconnection and Re-Connection. All consumers whose water service lines had been disconnected may re-apply subject to the payment of fees and all dues as reflected on the billing.
7. Request for Transfer of Water Meter. The consumer shall make a written request for the transfer of water meter to other location. There shall be no transfer of water meter if the applicant is not the owner and presentation of original receipt on the full payment of the transfer fee for the water meter at Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System.
All outstanding accounts of the consumer shall be fully settled first before the approval for the transfer of water meter be granted. Transfer fee covers the installation of the fittings.
All excavation and material costs beyond the limit of the standard design shall be shouldered by the consumer.
8. Disputed Bill. In the event that a complaint is made, the consumer shall be required to fill up the form stating the information and his complain at the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System within three (3) days from receipt of the Bill. Thereafter, the Meter Reader shall check the possible cause on the excessive bill. If found to have any leak, the meter will be removed with the written consent and approval by the consumer. The meter will pass thru a calibration with the presence of the consumer. Defective water meter shall be replaced by the Service Provider with the corresponding payment of the new unit.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 11
In case there is an error in reading, the average consumption of the Consumer for the previous three (3) months period will serve as basis for the computation.
Section 14. COMMERCIAL AND INDUSTRIAL SERVICE CONNECTION - Each parcel of land under separate ownership shall be provided with a separate water service line within the service area and any violation thereof shall be sufficient cause for the Service Provider to remove the water service line until said violation is corrected and paid the service connection fee.
# ARTICLE VIII
MAINTENANCE OF WATER SERVICE
Section 15. Maintenance of Water Service Connection - The service laterals extended from water main line to the water meter including the meter shall be maintained by the Service Provider. All pipes and fixtures extending from water meter or laying beyond the consumer's meter shall be maintained by the consumer.
Reported defective water meter shall be certified by the Plumber Foreman after passing through calibration and water testing. If the water meter shall be found defective, the Service Provider shall install the water meter as provided by the Consumer subject to the rules and regulations of this Ordinance.
# ARTICLE IX
WATER SANITATION
Section 16. WATER POTABILITY - The Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System shall ensure the consuming public on the water potability, free from any contaminations that may cause health problems. Chlorination and periodic/regular water testing shall be conducted in coordination with the accredited testing laboratory.
# ARTICLE X
WATER SUPPLY FOR PUBLIC PURPOSES
Section 17. Water Supply for Fire Hydrants - The Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System shall be responsible on the installation of fire hydrants in all strategic places within the service area of the Municipality
# ARTICLE XI
CONSERVATION AND PROTECTION OF WATER AND WATERSHED
Section 18. Guidelines for the Conservation and Protection of Water and Watershed:
1. Ensure water potability through establishment of buffer zones in every pump station of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System at least five hundred (500) meters away from the pump station.
2. The establishment of cemeteries and waste disposal areas must be 500 meters away from the water source or reservoir and be subjected to the rules and regulations of the Department of Health.
3. The application of agricultural fertilizers and pesticides maybe prohibited or regulated in areas where such application may cause pollution to the source of water supply.
4. The establishment of poultry and piggery for commercial base must be 500 meters away from the water source or pump station.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 12
5. The Local Economic Enterprise Management Office through the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System shall be responsible for watershed protection and shall undertake activities and measures in the protection and conservation of the watershed areas.
The office may establish partnership from the private sector for the said purpose.
6. To ensure sustainability of water source, no person or entity shall be allowed to drill wells for commercial purposes within 500- meter radius from the watershed area.
# ARTICLE XII
FEES AND CHARGES
Section 19. Imposition of Fees and Charges – The fees and charges herein shall be collected from the Consumer for the water services rendered by the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System, to wit:
Application Fee for Service Connection ₱ 100.00
Guarantee Deposit for every Connection ₱ 200.00
Guarantee Deposit of Temporary Connection for Construction ₱ 5,000.00
Transfer Fee of Water Meter ₱ 100.00
New Service Line (water meter) ₱ 1,500.00
Note: Price of the water meter will vary depending upon the purchase price from the Supplier.
For metered services:
a. Minimum charges for not more than 10 cubic meter per month
Residential Service ₱ 186.60
Institutional 100% of the residential service
Commercial Service
Category:
