Section 20. Discount Rate – A five (5) percent discount shall be provided to Senior Citizens and Persons With Disability (PWD).
# ARTICLE XIII
TIME AND MANNER OF PAYMENT
Section 21. TIME AND MANNER OF PAYMENT: All water bills, fees and charges are due and payable to the Office of the Municipal Treasurer's Office or thru the Authorized Representative of the Municipality.
The water bill shall be considered due on or before the 20th day of every month. Monthly water bills paid after the due date shall be subject to ten (10) percent surcharge.
If the due date falls on Saturdays, Sundays or Holidays, such due date shall be extended to Monday or the first working day after holiday.
# ARTICLE XIV
PROHIBITED ACTS
# Section 22. PROHIBITED ACTS
1. Illegal tapping and other illegal connections: Illegal tapping and tampering of water meter under this Ordinance shall be treated as criminal offense and sufficient ground for water disconnection.
2. Tampering of Water Meter: No person shall be allowed to operate the service cock or valve, main cock's gate or valve of the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System or interfere with meter or their connection, street main line or parts of the water system except the employee or representative of the Operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 14
3. Cross Connection. No person, firm or corporation shall install or maintain physical connection from a private source of water supply to the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System.
4. Using of jumper or any device whereby water is stolen;
5. Pilfering of water or water meter
## ARTICLE XV
## PENALTIES
Section 23. Any person who shall violate, disobey, refuse and/or neglect to comply with any of the provision of this ordinance shall be punished in accordance with the following penalties:
Penalties
1st offense - Reprimand
2nd offense - A fine of P1,000 and seminar
3rd offense - A fine of 2,500 and payment of damages
Corporation
- A fine of 2,500 and payment of damage;
- Revocation of business permit
Fines or penalty imposed herein shall be without prejudice to the administrative sanctions that maybe imposed to erring establishments.
## ARTICLE XVI
## FISCAL MANAGEMENT
Section 24. Fiscal Management - The fiscal management on the Operation of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks System which includes revenue collection, expenditures/disbursement, and control shall be governed by the existing Government Accounting and Auditing Rules and Regulations.
Section 25. All collection of fees and charges from the Operation of Waterworks System shall constitute a separate account for the specific economic enterprise and such to be utilized for its operational expenses, improvements, capital outlay and other relevant administrative expenses.
Section 26. All revenues collected using official receipts and cash tickets by the authorized Revenue Collector shall form part of the enterprise income.
Section 27. All income surplus derived from the operation of Sta. Cruz Waterworks System shall be flowed back to the Local Economic Enterprise Management Office to be used for the operation and improvement of public facilities.
Section 28. The Waterworks Superintendent is allowed to hold a petty cash for purposes of procuring supplies/ materials and other expenses urgently needed for repair, maintenance of the facilities for the waterworks services and other needs for the efficient operation of the Sta. Cruz Waterworks system subject to the rules and regulations of the Government Accounting System and Commission on Audit.
Waterworks Code of Sta. Cruz | Page 15
# ARTICLE XVII
FINAL PROVISIONS
Section 29. Final Penal Provisions – Violations in any of the existing provisions of this Ordinance shall be based on the Sanctions mentioned in the Articles of this Ordinance and upon discretion of the Court.
Section 30. Applicability Clause - Any resolutions, rules/regulations, ordinance or law consistent with this Ordinance/Code shall be valid and form part and supplementary to this Code.
Section 31. Separability Clause – If for any reasons, any part or provisions of this Code shall be held unconstitutional or invalid, other parts or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall continue to be in full force and effect.
Section 32. Repealing Clause - All existing ordinances relative or covering the herein economic enterprise of the Municipality prior to the enactment of this Code and other resolutions, rules and regulations or parts thereof, inconsistent herewith are hereby repealed or modified accordingly.
Section 33. Effectivity Clause - This Code shall take effect ten (10) days after its publication in one (1) newspaper of general circulation in the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur. Provided, however, should there be no newspaper of local circulation, the same shall be posted in at least two (2) conspicuous places within the territorial jurisdiction of the Municipality.
