# ENACTING AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT
SERVICES OFFICE (PESO) OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ,
DAVAO DEL SUR, PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS AND CREATING
THREE PLANTILLA POSITIONS THEREOF
WHEREAS, it is a declared policy of the state to promote full and equal employment opportunities for all, and for this purpose, strengthen and expand the existing employment facilitation service machinery of local government units;
WHEREAS, Republic Act No. 8759 otherwise known as the "Public Employment Service Office Act of 1999" mandates the creation of a Municipal Public Employment Service Office (PESO) in all LGUs in the country;
WHEREAS, the PESO Programs of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz under the Office of the Mayor has been existing for many years providing employment opportunities to job seekers through various job fairs and other local recruitment activities in coordination with the Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE), Technical Education School Development Authority (TESDA), Philippine Overseas Employment Agency (POEA) and other various private business sectors. However, its powers, functions and staffing pattern are not well defined thus necessitating the enactment of an ordinance creating thereby;
WHEREAS, the PESO shall ensure the prompt, timely and efficient delivery of employment services and information dissemination on the programs of the DOLE;
WHEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Charlotte F. Gallego, unanimously seconded by the members of the Sangguniang Bayan present, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session, to enact the following:
# MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 13
Series of 2020
# CREATING THE PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT SERVICES OFFICE (PESO)
OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR,
PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS AND CREATING
THREE (3) PLANTILLA POSITIONS THEREOF
Be it ordained by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, in session assembled that:
SECTION 1. Short Title. This Ordinance shall be known as "An Ordinance Creating the Public Employment Service Office (PESO) - Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur of 2020.
Municipal Ordinance No. 13 | Page 1
**SECTION 2. Declaration of Policy.** The Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, recognizes the importance and various objectives of the PESO, to ensure prompt, timely, and efficient delivery of employment services and the provision of information on other DOLE programs. Hence, the PESO shall:
a.) Provide a venue where people could explore simultaneously various employment options and actually seek assistance they prefer;
b.) Serve as referral and information center for various services and programs of the DOLE and other government agencies present in the area;
c.) Provide clients with adequate information on employment and labor market situation in the area; and
d.) Network with other PESO within the region, on employment for job exchange purposes.
**SECTION 3. Functions of the Public Employment Services Office (PESO)- Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur.** The PESO-Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur shall have the following functions:
a.) Encourage employers to regularly submit to the PESO a list of job vacancies in their respective establishments, in order to facilitate the exchange of labor market information services to job seekers, both for local and overseas employment, and recruitment assistance to employers;
b.) Develop and administer testing and evaluation instruments for effective job selection, training and counseling;
c.) Provide persons with entrepreneurship qualities access to various livelihood and self-employment programs offered by both government and non-government organizations at the provincial/cities/municipal/barangay levels by undertaking referrals for such programs;
d.) Undertake employability enhancement trainings/seminars for jobseekers, as well as for those who would like to change careers or enhance their employability, in coordination with the Municipal Skills Training Center;
e.) Provide employment and occupational counseling, career coaching, mass motivation and values development activities;
f.) Conduct pre-employment counseling and orientation to prospective local and overseas workers;
g.) Provide reintegration assistance services to returning Filipino migrant workers;
h.) Collect employment data and develop qualitative statistical indicators to facilitate the assessment of employment-related activities. It shall also serve as the data bank of the municipal government on Public Employment Services;
i.) Endeavor to look for market of local products and services and to provide for skill-product matching and technical support;
j.) Create linkages and partnerships with Non-Government Organizations (NGOs) and/or Civil Society Organizations;
k.) Coordinate with the different barangays in the Municipality for the inventory of skilled workers and professionals and transmit information to them relative to job vacancies and other employment services to job seekers;
1.) Encourage and assist the barangays within the Municipality to create Barangay Employment Assistance Center;
Municipal Ordinance No. 13 | Page 2
m.) Promote equal opportunity employment for qualified differently-abled persons;
n.) Promote equal rights to employment regardless of gender and sexual preferences;
o.) Prepare and submit to the local sanggunian an annual employment plan and budget including other regular funding sources and budgetary support of the PESO; and
p.) Perform such functions which willfully carry out the objectives of this Ordinance.
SECTION 4. Creation of Plantilla Positions. There is hereby a partial reorganization in the plantilla of personnel of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur in pursuance to Section 76 of RA 7160 by creating the PUBLIC EMPLOYMENT SERVICE OFFICE (PESO)- STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR under the Office of the Mayor. The following position titles are hereby created in conformity with the qualification standards set by the Civil Service Commission and its Salary Grade for local government units:
Title of Position
Salary Grade
a.) Senior Labor and Employment Officer (SG-19)
b.) Labor and Employment Officer II (SG-13)
c.) Labor and Employment Assistant (SG-9)
SECTION 5. Minimum Qualification Standards. The following qualification standards for the PESO Positions in the Local Government Units prescribed by the Civil Service Commission Memorandum Circular No. 20, Series of 2019 shall be required for the three plantilla positions, namely:
| Position Title | Education | Eligibility | Relevant Work Experience | Relevant Training |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| a.) Senior Labor and Employment Officer | Bachelor's Degree preferably in any of the following: Operations Management, Human Resource Management, Human Resource Development and/or allied fields | Career Service (Professional/ Second Level Eligibility | 2 Years of experience in program management relative to employment facilitation | 8 hours of relevant training on employment facilitation |
| b.) Labor and Employment Officer II | Bachelor's Degree preferably in any of the following: Operations Management, Human Resource Management, Human Resource Development and/or allied fields | Career Service (Professional/ Second Level Eligibility | 1 year of experience in program management relative to employment facilitation | 8 hours of relevant training on employment facilitation |
| c.) Labor and Employment Assistant | Completion of 2 years studies in college | Career Service (Sub Professional)/ First Level Eligibility | 1 year experience in employment facilitation | 4 hours of relevant training on employment facilitation |
Municipal Ordinance No. 13
Page 3
# SECTION 6. Duties & Responsibilities.
a.) The Senior Labor and Employment Officer shall perform the following:
a.1. Manage all technical and administrative activities of the office;
a.2. Develop action plans, proposals and other documents needed in the implementation of programs and services;
a.3. Identify training needs and arrange staff trainings as needed;
a.4. Responsible for informal stages of staff discipline, including coaching and counselling;
a.5. Maintain a systematic process flow to ensure the effective and efficient management of the office and avoid complaints from clients;
a.6. Conduct reviews of daily procedures and carry out remedial action(s);
a.7. Maintain effective communication with the Local Chief Executive to appraise and provide recommendations for policy directions;
a.8. Initiate and organize job fairs, provided that job fairs conducted by private entities or educational institutions shall be supervised and monitored by the PESO pursuant to DOLE guidelines;
a.9. Facilitate the conduct of local recruitment/special recruitment activities, in coordination with the POEA and in accordance with existing law, rules and regulations;
a.10. Initiate and organize livelihood and self-employment bazaars, in coordination with the government and non-government institutions undertaking livelihood and self-employment programs and services; and
a.11. Coordinate and monitor the implementation of government-funded infrastructure projects to provide recruitment assistance to contractors for their skilled and unskilled human resource requirement pursuant to RA 6685, otherwise known as the Workers Hiring in Infrastructure Projects (WHIP).
b.) The Labor and Employment Officer II shall perform the following:
b.1. Facilitate job solicitation from different private establishments;
b.2. Conduct registration of job applicants;
b.3. Interview and issue referral(s) to job applicants;
b.4. Conduct monitoring of placed job seekers;
b.5. Conduct Pre-Employment Seminar for Local Applicants (PESLA) and Pre-Employment Overseas Seminars (PEOS);
b.6. Assist in the conduct of Special Recruitment Activity (SRA) for overseas workers;
b.7. Conduct job fairs;
b.8. Facilitate Special Program for Employment of Students (SPES);
b.9. Encode registration forms of LMIS, SRS and Phil.Job.net;
b.10. Provide career coaching to incoming college students; and
b.11. Perform other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the immediate supervisor and/or LCE.
Municipal Ordinance No. 13 | Page 4
c.) The Labor and Employment Assistant shall perform the following:
c.1. Perform administrative functions of the office;
c.2. Under immediate supervision, assist in maintaining internal control system;
c.3. Keep all records orderly, prepare and encode reports, receive and control vouchers; and
c.4. Perform other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the supervisor and/or LCE.
**SECTION 7. Appropriations.** The budget necessary to carry out provisions of this Ordinance, following its enactment, shall be included in the ensuing Appropriation Ordinance, embodying the annual or supplemental budget, and every year hereafter, the same shall be included in the annual budget of the Municipal government of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz.
**SECTION 8. Separability Clause.** Should any section or provision of this Ordinance be declared void and ineffective by final judgment of a competent judicial authority, the other provisions hereof, not affected thereby, shall continue to be in full force and effect.
**SECTION 9. Repealing Clause.** This Ordinance expressly amends Municipal Ordinance No. 08, series of 2014 or the Revised Organizational Structure and Staffing Pattern of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, as amended, and Municipal Ordinance No. 11, Series of 2014, otherwise known as An Ordinance for Institutionalization of PESO in Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur;
**Section 10. Effectivity Clause.** This ordinance shall take effect upon approval.
**APPROVED**, by a unanimous vote of all members of the Sangguniang Bayan present.
