# **ENACTING AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE ENVIRONMENT
AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION AND
PROVIDING FOR ITS TASKS, FUNCTIONS, PERSONNEL AND
APPROPRIATION THEREOF AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES**
**WHEREAS**, Sec. 16, Article II of the Philippine Constitution guarantees the right of the people to a balanced and healthful ecology in accord with the rhythm and harmony of nature;
**WHEREAS**, RA 9003 otherwise known as the Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2000 which declared, among others, the policy of the State to adopt a systematic, comprehensive and ecological solid waste management program.
**WHEREAS**, Section 10 of the Act states that, pursuant to relevant provisions of RA 7160, the LGUs shall be primarily responsible for the implementation and enforcement of the provisions of this Act within their respective jurisdiction.
**WHEREAS**, Section 76 of RA 7160 otherwise known as the Local Government Code of 1991 states that every LGU shall design and implement its own organizational structure and staffing pattern taking into consideration its priority needs, service requirements and financial capability subject to the minimum standards and guidelines prescribed by the Civil Service Commission;
**WHEREAS**, Section 1, Article IV of Municipal Ordinance No. 06, s. 2011, provides that there shall be created a Municipal Environment and Natural Resources Office in this municipality which shall serve as the primary LGU Office responsible and accountable in the implementation of the Municipal Solid Waste Management Plan.
**WHEREAS**, the Environment and Natural Resources Management Section was created under the Municipal Agriculture Office by virtue of Municipal Ordinance No. 05, s. 2005 with plantilla positions of two (2) Environment Management Specialist I;
**WHEREAS**, to effect an efficient implementation and strict enforcement of the provisions of RA 9003 and other related statutes, it is necessary to rationalize the functions of the said work unit by upgrading such Section into a Division and augment the manpower requirement to pave the way for improved formulation, preparation, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of plans, policies and programs for the rehabilitation, protection, preservation, utilization and development of the municipality's environment, natural resources and solid waste management.
**WHEREFORE**, on motion of Hon. Ronald R. Cruda, seconded by Hon. Nestor B. Crave, it was
Municipal Ordinance No. 11 | Page 1
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to enact the following:
## MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 11
Series of 2020
# AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION AND PROVIDING FOR ITS TASKS, FUNCTIONS, PERSONNEL AND APPROPRIATION THEREOF AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES
Be it ordained by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, in session assembled that:
SECTION 1. TITLE. This Ordinance shall be known as an "AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION WITH FIVE (5) SECTIONS, AND PROVIDING FOR ITS RESPECTIVE TASKS, FUNCTIONS, PERSONNEL AND APPROPRIATION THEREOF AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES".
SECTION 2. POLICY. It is the policy of the municipality of Sta. Cruz to establish sustainable economic growth and development that is founded on good governance and on the protection and proper management of its environment and natural resources thereby promoting the right of the people to a balanced and healthful ecology in accord with the rhythm and harmony of nature.
SECTION 3. CREATION OF ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION. There is hereby created an ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION (ENRMD) consequently upgrading the ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT SECTION from THE MUNICIPAL AGRICULTURE OFFICE and placing it directly under the OFFICE OF THE MAYOR, and shall be composed of the following sections in accordance with the Ecological Solid Waste Management Ordinance of 2011 namely:
1) Mineral Resources and Industries Section
2) Protected Area, Wildlife and Forestry Section
3) Waste Management Section
4) Coastal Marine Management Section
5) Administrative Section
SECTION 4. OBJECTIVES. The ENVIRONMENT AND NATURAL RESOURCES MANAGEMENT DIVISION (ENRMD) shall be responsible for making the LGU of Santa Cruz responsive and compliant to the environmental concerns of this municipality, and be able to sustain environmental programs consistent with the municipality's economic thrust and development.
SECTION 5. GENERAL FUNCTIONS. The ENRMD shall perform the following functions:
1. Implement national laws and local ordinances regulating the emission/discharge of harmful substances to the atmosphere, and water systems, solid waste management policies and directives, and recommend for the apprehension of violators and abatement of the pollution;
Municipal Ordinance No. 11 | Page 2
2. Enforce the municipality's Ecological Solid Waste Management Program as embodied in Municipal Ordinance No. 06 s. 2011, Ecological Solid Waste Management Ordinance;
3. Manage the ecological and natural resources of the municipality, primarily promoting sustainability of local resources, such as but not limited to forests, watersheds, rivers, coasts, mangroves, and fishing grounds;
4. Implement programs for the protection and preservation of the environment, as well as rehabilitation of areas critically affected by industries, effects of natural calamities, result of man-made activities, etc.;
5. Provide technical assistance to the Local Chief Executive and the Legislative branch on policy and decision-making;
6. Conduct continuing education for the municipality's constituents stressing on environmental stewardship, awareness and responsibility;
7. Gather and maintain records of environmental data, activities, assets and compliments and evaluate the state of environment of the municipality;
8. Coordinate environmental activities within the territorial jurisdiction of the municipality and integrate it with the environmental master plan; and
9. Facilitate capacity building for local adaptation planning, implementation and monitoring of climate change initiatives in vulnerable communities and areas.
# **SECTION 6. SPECIFIC FUNCTIONS.** The following are the functions of the respective sections:
# **1) Mineral Resources and Industries Section**
a. Ensure optimization as well as promote conservation in the use and utilization of all mineral resources found within the territorial limits of the municipality consistent with RA 7942 otherwise known as the Philippine Mining Act of 1995;
b. Conduct inspection of commercial and industrial establishments regarding their air emissions and water discharges in accordance with RA 8749 otherwise known as the Philippine Clean Air Act of 1999 and RA 9275, the Philippine Clean Water Act;
c. Conduct survey and prepare inventory of establishments and industries concerning their emissions and discharges in coordination with the Geographic Information System (GIS);
d. In coordination with the Environment Management Bureau (EMB), implement laws for the achievement of clean environment and such other laws enacted to pursue EMB's mandate;
e. Recommend closure of business that repeatedly violates environmental laws and regulations;
f. Conduct sampling and analysis of pollutants and other toxic substances found in the environment;
g. In partnership with the Department of Science and Technology (DOST), Environment Management Bureau (EMB) and other government agencies, increase the capacity of the LGU in technical know-how and laboratory sciences.
h. Collect and collate data from various organizations/institutions who sample, analyze and/or monitor pollution from air, water and/or land; and propose means for the collection of data, when not immediately available from other sources on the ambient environment.
Municipal Ordinance No. 11 | Page 3
i. In coordination with the Department of the Environment and Natural Resources (DENR), implement mining and quarrying laws and such other laws that would be enacted to pursue DENR's mandate;
# 2) Protected Area, Wildlife and Forestry Section
a. Implementation of programs and rehabilitation in conservation of hotspots and the conservation of rare and endangered species of flora and fauna in areas identified and delineated by the DENR, pursuant to Section 3.2 (a) of DAO 30, Series of 1992;
b. Coordinate the efforts of the municipality and other LGU's, national government agencies, NGO's and other organizations aimed at addressing environmental issues and collaborate with such organizations in the implementation of projects and programs related to environmental protection climate change adaptation and mitigation measures;
c. Implementation of community based forestry projects, such as integrated social forestry, establishment of new regular reforestation projects, except those located in protected areas and critical watersheds, completed family and community based contract reforestation projects, subject to policies and procedures prescribed by the DENR, Forest Land Management Agreements, in accordance with DAO No. 71, Series of 1990 and other guidelines that the DENR may adopt and Community Forestry Projects;
d. Establishment and maintenance of tree parks, greenbelts and other tourist attractions through beautification projects, except those in protected areas and the collection of fees for their services and the use of facilities established therein;
