# ENACTING AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE GENDER AND DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (GADD) OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS AND CREATING FIVE PLANTILLA POSITIONS THEREOF
WHEREAS, Article 2, Section 14 of the 1987 Philippine Constitution states that the State recognizes the role of women in nation-building, and shall ensure the fundamental equality before the law of women and men;
WHEREAS, Section 36 of Republic Act No. 9710, otherwise known as the Magna Carta of Women (MCW), provides that all government departments, including their attached agencies, offices, bureaus, state universities and colleges, government-owned and -controlled corporations, local government units and all other government instrumentalities shall adopt gender mainstreaming as a strategy to promote women's human rights and eliminate gender discrimination in their systems, structures, policies, programs, processes, and procedures;
WHEREAS, Joint Memorandum Circular No. 2013-01 of PCW-DILG-DBM-NEDA provides that, where feasible, the LGU may establish a GAD Office or unit under the Office of the Local Chief Executive that will support and coordinate all GAD-related PPAs and concerns of the LGU GFPS;
WHEREAS, Section 76 of Republic Act 7160, otherwise known as the Local Government Code, recognizes the power of the local government unit to design and implement its own organizational structure and staffing pattern taking into consideration its service requirements and financial capability, subject to the minimum standards and guidelines prescribed by the Civil Service Commission;
WHEREAS, the LGU-Sta. Cruz finds it beneficial to create an organic unit, which will cater the wide-ranging issues pertaining to gender and development and to properly institute and implement GAD programs, projects and activities (PPAs) in accordance with the GAD budget policy of the Philippine General Appropriations Act that directs all agencies of government to allocate a minimum of five percent (5%) of the total annual budgets for gender mainstreaming and gender-responsive policies, programs and projects;
NOW THEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Charlotte F. Gallego, duly seconded by Hon. Ronald R. Cruda, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled in session to enact the following municipal ordinance:
Municipal Ordinance No. 10 | Page 1
# MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 10
Series of 2020
# AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE GENDER AND DEVELOPMENT DIVISION (GADD) OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, PRESCRIBING ITS FUNCTIONS AND CREATING FIVE PLANTILLA POSITIONS THEREOF
SECTION 1. Creation of Gender and Development Division. It is hereby created the Gender and Development Division (GADD) of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, which shall be responsible in carrying out of the devolved powers set forth in Republic Act No. 7160, Republic Act No. 9710, and other Gender and Development related laws.
SECTION 2. Functions of Gender and Development Division (GADD). The Division shall:
a. Ensure the implementation of Municipal Ordinance No. 02, series of 2012 or the GENDER AND DEVELOPMENT (GAD) CODE OF STA. CRUZ;
b. Mainstream gender and development programs by way of the following, without prejudice to other mainstreaming approaches that the Division may adopt, viz:
b.1. Gender-Sensitive Watch. A system of services and facilities in order to monitor the status of men and women in the municipality, wherein all departments and agencies therein shall develop conceptual and practical methodologies for incorporating gender perspectives into all aspects of economy and policy-making. It shall collect gender and age disaggregated data on poverty situation and all aspects of economic activity and develops qualitative statistical indicators to facilitate the assessment of economic performance from a gender fair perspective. It shall also serve as the data bank of the municipal government on gender and development;
b.2. Legal Aid Services Check. A coordinated service for any legal action needed in protecting women, children, and special group of person's rights shall be installed;
b.3. Advocacy. A coordinated advocacy and campaign on all forms of discrimination and violence against any person shall be programmed; and
b.4. Gender Sensitive Sustainable Project Development. A system of appraisal of projects to determine sustainable impact on persons;
c. Develop GAD capacity development programs such as gender sensitivity, gender analysis, gender-responsive planning and budgeting and gender audit, among others, that support continuing gender education, updating and enhancing skills customized according to the functions of the Gender Focal Point System (GFPS);
d. Conduct periodic monitoring and evaluation of their GFPS and shall undertake measures to address possible issues hindering the performance of their functions in accordance with the Magna Carta of Women and other GAD-related laws, policies and plans;
e. Lead in mainstreaming gender perspective in agency, department and barangay policies, plans and programs. In the process, they shall ensure the assessment of the gender-responsiveness of systems, structures, policies, programs, processes, and procedures of the agency, department and barangay are based on the priority needs and concerns of constituencies and employees and the formulation of recommendations, including their implementation;
f. Prepare annual performance-based GAD Plans;
Municipal Ordinance No. 10 | Page 2
g. Prepare and consolidate the annual agency GAD Accomplishment Report and other GAD Reports that may be required under the law;
h. Monitor the effective implementation of GAD-related policies and the annual GAD Plans, Programs and Budget;
i. Strengthen the external link with other agencies or organizations working on women's rights and gender and development to harmonize and synchronize GAD efforts at various levels of governance; and
j. Promote and actively pursue the participation of women and gender advocates, other civil society groups and private organizations in the various stages of the development planning cycle, giving special attention to the marginalized sectors.
SECTION 3. Creation of Plantilla Positions. There is hereby a partial reorganization in the plantilla of personnel of the Municipal Government of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, in pursuance to Section 76 of RA 7160, by creating the GENDER AND DEVELOPMENT DIVISION under the Office of the Mayor. The following position titles are hereby created in conformity with the qualification standards set by the Civil Service Commission and its index of Salary Grade for local government units:
| Title of Position | Salary Grade |
| --- | --- |
| a. Administrative Officer V | (SG-18) |
| b. Planning Officer I | (SG-11) |
| c. Planning Officer I | (SG-11) |
| d. Clerk III | (SG-6) |
| e. Clerk II | (SG-4) |
SECTION 4. Minimum Qualification Standards. The qualification standards prescribed by the Civil Service Commission (CSC) and the Qualification Standards for Newly Created Positions in the Philippine Commission for Women, whichever is applicable, shall be required for the five plantilla positions.
# SECTION 5. Duties & Responsibilities.
a. The Administrative Officer V shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:
a.1. Performs the functions and responsibilities inherent to the Division in providing technical and administrative support to the Local Chief Executive (LCE), particularly those which have to do with Gender and Development (GAD) Programs, as mandated by the agency's GAD Code, which includes, among others, the following:
a.1.1. Acts as Head Secretariat for the GAD Focal Point System (GFPS) and to other ad hoc committees created specifically to carry out the provisions of the GAD Code, by providing administrative, operational and coordinative support thereof;
a.1.2. Initiates multi-sectoral capacity building activities for GAD mainstreaming efforts;
a.1.3. Spearheads information dissemination and awareness in building and in the production of Information, Education, Communication (IEC) tools, such as, but not limited to regular publications, research and monitoring reports, municipal gender profiling, advocacy materials, audio-visual materials, as well as the identification and maintenance of resource persons and trainers for GAD Learning and Development (L&D) opportunities;
Municipal Ordinance No. 10 | Page 3
a.1.4. Initiates the establishment and maintenance of a GAD database which will serve as basis for gender-responsive planning, programming and policy formulation;
a.1.5. Facilitates the holding of GAD-related assemblies for consultation of gender issues and for the registration and election of women NGO/PO representatives, subject to pertinent regulations that the Sanggunian may promulgate; and
a.1.6. Undertakes all other works required for the effective and efficient discharge of the GFPS functions as provided under the Guidelines on the Localization of Magna Carta of Women and other pertinent laws and issuances.
a.2. Formulates measures, strategies and policy alternatives to attain gender mainstreaming on local policies through the conduct of policy research, sectoral analysis and other related studies, proposes the same to the Sanggunian for due adoption and/or to the LCE for approval and implements thereof accordingly;
a.3. Conducts review of relevant development plans and policies by way of workshops and consultations with key officials and stakeholders;
a.4. Takes lead in the planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation (PIME) of programs, plans and activities (PPAs) appropriated and/or attributed to the GAD Program undertaken by various departments/work units of the agency;
a.5. Supervises efforts to ensure the timely consolidation and submission of the agency's annual GAD Plan and Budget (GPB), GAD Accomplishment Report (GAD AR) and other GAD reports required to the appropriate oversight agencies;
a.6. Develops and initiates programs that advocate gender-sensitive and gender-responsive governance; and
a.7. Performs other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the LCE.
b. The Planning Officer I (Planning and Implementing Section) shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:
b.1. Facilitates the planning of programs, plans and activities (PPAs) appropriated and/or attributed to the GAD Program undertaken by various departments/work units of the agency and coordinates the implementation thereof with the concerned implementing work unit;
b.2. Performs secretariat functions for the GAD Focal Point System-Technical Working Group (GFPS-TWG) by providing administrative, operational and coordinative support thereto;
b.3. Assists the GFPS Executive Committee and the GFPS-TWG in the performance of their roles and responsibilities, specifically on the provision of administrative and logistical services; preparation of meeting agenda; and documentation of GFPS meetings and other GAD-related activities;
b.4. Collaborates with the supervisor in formulating measures, strategies and policy alternatives to attain gender mainstreaming on local policies through the conduct of policy research, sectoral analysis and other related studies;
b.5. Takes effort in ensuring the timely consolidation and submission of the agency's annual GAD Plan and Budget (GPB) and other GAD-related Reports to the appropriate oversight agencies;
b.6. Facilitates the conduct of related learning and development activities for GAD mainstreaming efforts;
Municipal Ordinance No. 10 | Page 4
b.7. Advocates gender-sensitive and gender-responsive governance; and
b.8. Performs other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the immediate supervisor and/or LCE.
c. The Planning Officer I (Monitoring and Evaluation Section) shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:
c.1. Facilitates the monitoring of programs, plans and activities (PPAs) appropriated and/or attributed to the GAD Program undertaken by various departments/work units of the agency and coordinates the evaluation thereof with the concerned implementing work unit;
c.2. Performs secretariat functions for the GAD Monitoring and Evaluation (GAD M&E) Team by providing administrative, operational and coordinative support thereto;
c.3. Assists the GFPS Executive Committee and the GAD M&E in the performance of their roles and responsibilities, specifically in monitoring the implementation of the annual GPB and assessing the states of the LGU's institutional mechanism on gender mainstreaming;
c.4. Takes effort in ensuring the timely consolidation and submission of the agency's annual GAD Accomplishment Report (GAD AR) and other related M & E Reports to the appropriate oversight agencies;
c.5. Formulates the tool for collecting relevant data and information for the GAD Database;
c.6. Facilitates the conduct of periodic gender analysis of the agency's programs, projects and activities appropriated and/or attributed to GAD through the administration of the Harmonized Gender and Development Guidelines (HGDG), Gender Mainstreaming Evaluation Framework (GMEF) Matrix and other evaluation tools as may be deemed applicable;
c.7. Advocates gender-sensitive and gender-responsive governance; and
c.8. Performs other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the immediate supervisor and/or LCE.
d. The Clerk III shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:
d.1. Receives, releases, records the incoming and outgoing communications for proper records management by adopting a workable system;
d.2. Types and/or encodes correspondence, reports and other pertinent documents;
d.3. Files records according to the established procedures;
d.4. Provides clerical/secretarial support to the GAD Focal Point System (GFPS) as instructed; and
d.5. Performs other related functions as may be directed from time to time by the immediate supervisor.
e. The Clerk II shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:
e.1. Receives, releases, records the incoming and outgoing communications for proper records management by adopting a workable system;
e.2. Types and/or encodes correspondence, reports and other pertinent documents;
e.3. Files records according to the established procedures; and
