AFFIRMING THE INTEREST OF THE LOCAL GOVERNMENT UNIT OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR AND AUTHORIZING MAYOR JEROME A. UNDALOK TO APPLY, NEGOTIATE AND PARTICIPATE IN THE MINDANAO BASIC URBAN SERVICES SECTOR PROJECT (MBUSSP), AND TO BORROW FUNDS FROM THE MUNICIPAL DEVELOPMENT FUND OFFICE (MDFO) UNDER THE DEPARTMENT OF FINANCE (DOF), AND UNDERTAKE OTHER ACTS NECESSARY TO THE EFFECTIVE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE PROJECT RE: CONSTRUCTION OF PUBLIC MARKET
WHEREAS, there is a need to relocate the old public market from its present site to an area near and/or adjacent to the Municipal Integrated Transport Terminal to complement the latter,
WHEREAS, aside from the complimentary advantage of a new public market to the integrated transport terminal, the following benefits may be derived:
1. the old market area will be decongested and can give way for other developments both in the government and private sector;
2. the relocation of the public market to the new area will boast the utility of the municipal integrated terminal as a government facility and provide more entrepreneurial activities in the otherwise sleepy commercial area;
3. the project will lure more commercial investments to the municipality and enhance its resource development efforts.
WHEREAS, that the Construction of Public Market proposed for financing under the MBUSSP Project is included in the approved local development plan/annual investment plan of the LGU of Sta. Cruz;
WHEREAS, in as much as the LGU has limited financial resources to support the proposed project, there is a need for the latter to borrow funds from the Municipal Development Fund Office (MDFO) under the Department of Finance (DOF);
WHEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Oliver O. Enot, unanimously seconded, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, assembled in session to affirm the interest of the Municipality of Sta. Cruz to participate in the MBUSSP Project to finance its proposed Construction of Public Market,
RESOLVED FURTHER, to authorize and empower the incumbent Local Chief Executive (LCE), Hon. Jerome A. Undalok, or his successor, for and in behalf of the LGU of Sta. Cruz to undertake the following:
- To apply, negotiate, enter into contract, execute, sign memoranda of agreement, local agreements, loan documents, project agreements, credit facilities deeds, and other papers with the Municipal Development Fund Office-Department of Finance (MDFO-DOF), for financing/funding of the proposed Construction of the Public Market, including amendments, renewal and/or extension thereof under such terms and conditions as may be agreed upon by MDFO-DOF, under the MBUSSP-MDFO Project;
1
- To participate in the MBUSSP-MDFO Project and cooperate in the implementation of the subprojects proposed for financing under the MBUSSP Project and avail of financing and/other available packages by the MDFO-DOF;
- To undertake other acts necessary to the effective implementation of the proposed Construction of Public Market,
RESOLVED FURTHERMORE, to authorize the incumbent Local Chief Executive, Hon. Mayor Jerome A. Undalok or his successor, for and in behalf of the LGU of Sta. Cruz, to affirm and undertake the following commitments required by the MBUSSP Project:
a. To appropriate LGU equity required and proceeds of the loan and grant by the proposed subproject;
b. To appropriate funds for the required insurance cost which is approximately 2.5% of the building and equivalent cost;
c. To provide maintenance trust fund for the completed local subprojects;
d. To provide funds for the annual amortization for loan repayments until the contracted loan is fully paid;
e. To authorize the Municipal Development Fund Office-Department of Finance to intercept the Internal Revenue Allotment (IRA) of the Municipality equivalent to the amount due in case of default in the payment of loan amortization and/or in the case of unliquidated financial obligations without prejudice to the filing of appropriate charges;
f. To conduct credible public hearings and enact ordinances relative to the imposition of fees and charges;
g. To provide a local subproject office and designate a local subproject officer and technical staff as may be necessary for the execution of the subproject;
h. To provide office space and facilities and all other support services as may be needed;
i. To conduct public hearings to ensure the acceptability of the subproject; and
j. To authorize the LCE to enter into contract with the wining bidders for civil works, consultancy, procurement of goods/equipment and other agreements required to be done.
RESOLVED FINALLY, to furnish the Municipal Development Fund Office-Department of Finance (MDFO-DOF) and the MBUSSP Project Development Office-Department of Interior and Local Government with a copy of this resolution.
