INDORSING APPROVAL OF HOUSE BILL NO. 2349 RE: ESTABLISHING A SCHOOL OF ARTS AND TRADE IN THE MUNICIPALITY OF STA. CRUZ, DAVAO DEL SUR
WHEREAS, the Municipality of Sta. Cruz has been declared an Industrial Zone of Davao del Sur by virtue of its approved Comprehensive Town Plan and Zoning Ordinance;
WHEREAS, the advent of industrialization in Sta. Cruz also calls for the training of skilled labor now in order to meet the labor needs of the industries that will come into the area;
WHEREAS, this skilled labor requirements of industries can be provided by the feeder schools located in the area which only offer a general secondary course;
WHEREAS, a post-secondary school in the area that will offer technical-vocational courses for the meantime and eventually undergraduate courses in the future will augment the skills of high school graduates in the Municipality who are taught only the basic rudiments of technical education by their respective Secondary Schools;
WHEREAS, Congressman Alejandro D. Almendras of the 1st District of Davao del Sur had filed House Bill No. 2349, establishing a school of Arts and Trade in the municipality of Sta. Cruz in answer to this need;
WHEREAS, the said Bill which has been approved in the First Reading is now referred to the Committee on Education particularly to the Committee in Organization of New Schools for deliberations;
WHEREAS, this bill is approved in the Second and Third Reading in the House of Representatives will answer the strong clamor of the different sectors of this municipality for the establishment of a tertiary school that will provide its Youth skills for ready employment by the industries and for livelihood;
NOW THEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Philip R. Rizada, Sr., unanimously seconded, it was
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz assembled in session, to strongly indorse for approval of House Bill No. 2349 authored by Hon. Alejandro D. Almendras, Congressman of the 1st District of Davao del Sur, for the establishment of a School of Arts and Trade in the municipality of Sta. Cruz;
RESOLVED FURTHER, to seek similar indorsement for approval of said bill from the Division and Regional Offices of the Department of Education and Culture and Sports, and from the different Sectors in the municipality;
RESOLVED FURTHERMORE, to inform the Speaker of the House of Representatives, Hon. Jose de Venecia, thru the Committee on Education of the said Body, the Senate President, Hon. Edgardo Angar, thru the Committee on Education of the House of Senate, that the local government unit has allocated a site for the establishment of such school in its approved comprehensive Town Plan and Zoning Ordinance;
