WHEREAS, pursuant to the provision of Section 9(b) and
Section 19 Article VIII of PD 807, the Civil Service Commission in its Resolution 83-343 prescribing Rule on Promotion governing the lower progression of employee in the Career Service;
WHEREAS, Section 10 PD 807 requires each ministry or agency of the government to establish a Merit Promotion Plan and System of Ranking Position;
NOW THEREFORE, on motion of Hon. Manuelito D. Jumilla, duly seconded by Hon. Ignatius R. Bajo,
RESOLVED, as it is hereby resolved by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, to adopt and approve the following Municipal Ordinance, to wit:
MUNICIPAL ORDINANCE NO. 05
ESTABLISHING A MERIT PROMOTION PLAN AND A SYSTEM OF RANKING POSITION.
Be it ordained by the Sangguniang Bayan of Sta. Cruz, Davao del Sur, assembled, that:
SECTION I - Promotion - is the advancement of an employee from one position to another with an increase of duties and responsibilities as authorized by law, and usually accompanied by an increase of salary;
SECTION II - Whenever a position in the first level becomes vacant, the employees in the department or agency who occupy position deemed to be next-in-rank the vacancy shall be considered for promotion. In the second level, those employees in the government service who occupy next-in-rank position shall be considered for promotion;
SECTION III - A next-in-rank position refers to a position which, by reasons of the hierarchical arrangement of position in the department of agency in the government, is determine to be in the nearest degree of relationship to a higher position taking into account the following:
- a) Organization structure as reflected in the approved organizational chart;
- b) Classification and/or functional relationship;
- c) Salary and/or large allocation.
SECTION IV - An employee who holds a next-in-rank position who is deemed the most competent and qualified, possesses appropriate Civil Service eligibility, and meets the other conditions for promotion shall be promoted to the higher position when it becomes vacant. However, the appointing authority may promote an employee who is not next-in-rank but who possesses superior qualification and competence compared to next-in-rank employee who merely meets the maximum requirements for the positions;
- 2 -
SECTION V - The comparative degree of competence and qualification of employee shall be determine by the extent which they meet the following requirements:
a) Performance - this shall be based on the last two performance rating of the employee, however, no employee shall be considered for promotion unless the last two performance rating is at least very satisfactory;
b) Education and Training - these shall include educational background and the successful completion of training courses, scholarships, training grants and others. Such education and training must be relevant to the duties of the position to be filled;
c) Experience and Outstanding Accomplishments - these shall include occupational history, work experience and accomplishments worthy of special commendations;
d) Personality Traits and Physical Characteristics - these refer to the physical fitness, attitudes and personality traits of the individual which must have a bearing on the position to be filled;
e) Potential - this takes into account the employees capability not only to perform the duties and assume the responsibilities of the position to be filled but also those of higher and more responsible position.
SECTION VI - No other Civil Service Eligibility shall be required for promotion to higher position in the same level and within the same or functionally related grouping of positions;
SECTION VII - To ensure objectivity in promotion, a Selection Board shall be established in every department or sections which shall be responsible for the adoption of a formal screening procedure and formulation of criteria for the evaluation of candidates for promotions;
SECTION VIII - In filling supervisory positions the selection board shall develop criteria for managership and leadership which shall constitute one of the instruments for selection of candidates for promotions;
SECTION IX - Each department or sections shall establish a qualification index of all employees;
SECTION X - Each Department or Sections shall have a merit promotion plan and a system of ranking Positions;
SECTION XI - All appointment involved in a chain of promoting must be submitted simultaneously for approval by the Commission (CSC);
SECTION XII - The incumbent of a position that has been reclassified as upgraded due to increase in responsibilities and/or changes in nature of duties, shall be issued a permanent appointment if he is qualified and possesses appropriate eligibility for the position;
SECTION XIII - When an employee who is legitimately entitled to promotion has a pending administrative case, the position to which he should have been promoted shall not be filled until after the administrative case shall have been finally decided;
- 3 -
SECTION XIV - Within 15 days from notice of the issuance of an appointment, a next-in-rank employee who is competent and qualified and who feels aggressive by the promotions of another may file a protest to the department or sections head who shall make a decision within 30 days from the receipt of the protest;
SECTION XV - An employee who still not satisfies with the decision of the Board may appeal to the Civil Service Commission 15 days from receipt of the decision. The Commission shall make a decision within 60 days from the date of receipt of approval;
SECTION XVI - In all instances only are positions for reconsiderations shall be entertained. The petitioner shall point out errors in the original decisions and he shall present new evidences;
SECTION XVII - Failure to file protest or appeal a petition for reconsideration within the prescribed period shall be deemed a waiver of such right;
SECTION XVIII - An appointment though contested shall take effect immediately upon its issuance if the appointee assume the duties of the position and the appointee is entitled to receive the salary attached to the position;
SECTION XIX - This ordinance shall take effect upon approval.
